2 TYPE King Haakon V tried to delete his name and mentions of him
2 NOTE Description: When King Eirik died in 1299, his younger brother, King Haakon V, took the throne. Haakon despised how much control Audun held over the realm and its treasury. The king launched an aggressive campaign to take back royal authority and c
3 CONC ompletely crush Audun's legacy: 
3 CONT 
3 CONT The Power Threat: Audun had been the co-ruler of the kingdom and effectively ran the treasury. King Haakon wanted to prove that no nobleman was untouchable.
3 CONT 
3 CONT The Execution Method: Normally, noblemen were granted the quick and honorable death of being beheaded by a sword. By hanging him on a rope instead, the king him as a lowly, common thief in the public eye.
3 CONT 
3 CONT Wiped from the Records: The King seized all of Audun's massive estates and lands. Crucially, the royal court wiped out any official mention of the specific crimes Audun was charged with. Historians believe it was likely a mix of political oppositio
3 CONC n and perceived financial corruption.
