1 NAME Hughleik /Hegranes/
1 NAME Hughleik /Hegranes/
1 SEX M
1 OCCU Hugleik was a lower nobleman and member of the royal court (hird) of King Håkon Håkonsson. Hugleik of Hegranes was a royal advisor serving in the king's hird (the royal court and advisory body) for roughly 20 to 30 years, spanning from the 1240
2 CONC s to the 1260s.
2 DATE from 1240 to 1260s
1 BIRT
2 DATE Abt 1222
2 PLAC Hegranes,,, Norge
3 MAP
4 LATI 62.0
4 LONG 10.0
1 DEAT Y
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Affiliation
2 NOTE Description: A Stepping Stone: While Hugleik was a respected advisor, he was not the most powerful man at court. However, his loyalty and connections allowed him to secure a world-class education for his son, Audun Hugleiksson.
3 CONT 
3 CONT The Ultimate Payoff: Because of Hugleik's service, his son Audun went on to become a baron, tax minister, and the ultimate right-hand advisor to the next two kings of Norway, serving as the co-ruler of the kingdom for over two decades!
