2 NPFX JARL "EARL"
2 NOTE @NFS1135@
2 NICK Haakon the Crazy 
1 SEX M
1 EVEN
2 TYPE BIOGRAPHY
2 NOTE Description: Håkon Galen was a skilled military leader, but his Swedish origins were sometimes held against him in Norway. His legacy continued through his son, Knut Håkonsson, who later made claims to the Norwegian throne
2 NOTE @NFS1139@
1 EVEN
2 TYPE MILITARY+AND+POLITICAL+CAREER
2 NOTE Description: 1193: First mentioned in the sagas as a Birkebeiner warrior, fighting for King Sverre against Harald Maddadsson, Earl of Orkney.  1204: After King Håkon III died, Håkon was made leader of the army, given the title jarl, and named ste
3 CONC ward of the kingdom during the minority of King Guttorm Sigurdsson.  1204–1208: Fought against the Bagler faction, led by Erling Steinvegg and Philippus Simonsson, until the Kvitsøy settlement ended the conflict
2 NOTE @NFS1140@
1 BIRT
2 DATE about 1173
