2 TYPE Heraldic+symbol+-Pukehorn
2 NOTE Description: A Pukehorn , is in heraldry an upturned eagle wing, sometimes slightly curved or twisted, to fit into the coat of arms. Some clans have carried the Pukehorn as an inherited ancestral weapon, including the older Puke family .   Pukehor
3 CONC n is called in heraldry an upturned eagle wing, inherited within a family or carried by people who called themselves Puke . Pukehorn as a coat of arms seems to have been surrounded by special mysticism and symbolic value, and the nickname Puke , wh
3 CONC ich is said to mean the evil one and was an older name for the devil , has been worn by several Scandinavians during the Middle Ages, who carried an upturned wing in their coat of arms. they were related to each other, while their relatives normall
3 CONC y carried the family's weapons. The puke horn was carried, for example, by unrelated people who called themselves Puke or Puki is Guttorm and Sigurd Puki in Loms parish in Norway, Paul Puke in Romerige .
