1 SOUR @SFS1038@
2 PAGE In 1297, Queen Isabella and King Eirik had their only child, the daughter Ingebjørg (1297 – ca. 1357). 
3 CONT Ingebjørg Eiriksdatter married the Swedish duke Valdemar, and his brother Erik married Ingebjørg's cousin Ingebjørg Håkonsdatter in a double wedding in 1312. Ingebjørg Eiriksdatter also became an early widow, but continued to live in Sweden. I
3 CONC n 1357, a Swedish document states that the widow Duchess Ingebjørg's mother will inherit from her daughter, who was the Duchess of Öland when she died. So it seems that Isabella survived her daughter.
