0 @IFS2473@ INDI
1 NAME Mattis /Torgeirson Tufte/
1 SEX M
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Notes
2 NOTE Description: Mattis Torgeirsson is mentioned as a magistrate in the Skiens county in a letter dated 18 June 1417 and again in two letters dated 28 February 1440. In a letter dated 25 February 1439, wife Sigrid Niklisdatter (Galle) at Brunla - Markv
3 CONC ard Buk's widow - acknowledges the receipt of a letter from the farmers in Gjerpen skibrede, which they had sent her with Mattis Torgeirsson, "hvilket ek let mik væl at nøgiæ eftir thy min herre konungin oc rikis radh med honom finnæ fore rett
3 CONC æ."  Mattis has thus, as the farmers' envoy, negotiated with wife Sigrid, and probably also with the Council of State, to achieve a settlement on the occasion of the Gjerpen residents' participation in Hallvard Graatop's rebellion and the plunderi
3 CONC ng of Brunla in 1438, and has undoubtedly been one of the most prominent men in skibrede. His seal. which is preserved under one of the letters from 1440, contains a home mark. Nothing further is known about his origin and family relations at prese
3 CONC nt.."  This is what Henning Sollied writes about Mattis Torgeirsson in Norsk Slektshistorisk Tidsskrift IX p. 112. He believes that Mattis Torgeirsson is probably the father of Nils Mattisson. There is no irrefutable evidence of that. But Nils Matt
3 CONC isson was a wealthy man, with a high reputation in Gjerpen. It is natural to assume that his father was too. And then there are no other alternatives with the Mattis name in Gjerpen.
