0 @NFS349@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Ølver/Olfvir was the father of Herr Svale Ølversson and his sisters.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The current prevailing theory is that Herr Svale was the father-in-law, and not the father, of herr Otte Rømer - which would mean the name Rømer has been falsely attributed to both Svale and Ølver. The patronymic 'Henningsson' is also very quest
1 CONC ionable; it would only apply if Ølver was certainly the son of Henning - while, as stated above, it seems more like his grandson married into Henning's descendant's family.(Østenstad-1 08:27, 9 December 2018 (UTC))
0 @NFS350@ NOTE Family Search recommends that unless you know the name, the name fields should be left blank.  But once you create an ID number, something has to go in a space.
1 CONT 
1 CONT For the Search engine process to work the best, a ? should not be used.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT I use unknown when I have no other choice when fixing all kinds of names including Mrs.  That title was never used in Norway.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The title Mrs.with the husband's full name is used in FamilySearch for their temple program to work for an unknown wife. Please, do not change. Instead add an alternative wife with a new id number and use unknown or datter if you want. By checkin
1 CONC g the box, that will appear on your own familytree. The temple program is already started for this woman and it will be disrupted by adding unknown or datter. This is what we teach at FamilySearch centers throughout the world. (I did not write th
1 CONC e first part here).
