0 @NFS454@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Åmund Einarsson Hildugard was born in 1210 in Bergen, Hordaland, Norway, into a lineage that appears to have held regional influence during the early 13th century.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Titles and Roles
1 CONT Åmund is noted to have held the title of Lagmann (lawman), a prestigious legal and administrative role in medieval Norway. He served as:
1 CONT    - Lagmann in Oslo (1279)
1 CONT    - Lagmann in Bergen and Tønsberg These positions placed him at the heart of legal governance in key Norwegian cities, indicating his prominence in judicial and civic affairs.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Property and Land Transfers
1 CONT A note in the record mentions Åmund's involvement in a land exchange:
1 CONT “Makeskiftede 'Bjørke' på Follo mot Holter i Nes, Akershus.” This suggests he traded property in Follo for land in Holter, Nes—an area with ties to noble and ecclesiastical estates.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Åmund is associated with the Kyrningen kin group in Oslo and may be a progenitor of the Hvam-Sta lineage. His alternate name, Lagmann Amund Audunsson Holter, hints at connections to the Holter estate and possibly to the Audunsson family, which ma
1 CONC y have held judicial or noble status.
