1 CONC ay 2011BiographyBishop Håkon is said in some texts to be the son of Torer Audunsson Tinghatt and his wife, an unknown Haftorsdatter,[1] while other literature states that Håkon's parentage is unknown. [2]He was the father of Tore Håkonsson/Bisko
1 CONC psson, mentioned between 1271 and 1317 and one of the most prominent men in Norway at the time.[2]He was the bishop in Oslo from 1248.[2]He was on good terms with the king, and was instrumental in bringing Ingeborg, daughter of Erik Plovpenning, fr
1 CONC om Denmark to Norway to marry king Magnus Lagabøte.[2]He donated several large landholdings to the diocese in Oslo in 1264; in return, the clergy were to say masses over the bishop and his mother when he died, and give food to 30 paupers and gift
1 CONC s to the churches in Oslo on his death day.[2]He became the arch bishop of Nidaros on Shrove Thursday, 14 April, in 1267.[2]He died 18 Aug 1267.[2]Sources? Nes på Romerike. 6, pp. 292-293.? 2.0 2.1 2.2 2.3 2.4 2.5 2.6 Håkon - Norsk Biografisk Lek
