0 @NFS628@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Two Guttorms were merged in this name. GUTTORM IVARSSON Norheim is the correct one. Norheim is the farm name. Guttorm Kalvsen Torsnes is not a part of this family.
1 CONT 
1 CONT All that is known about Guttorm comes from the probate held in Norheim on February 20, 1306 after his death. His name is Guttorm Ivarsson and he comes from Norheim. He had a son named Ivar. A daughter named Ingebjørg was married to Peter Joensso
1 CONC n Sandven. A second daughter, whose name might have been Sigurd, was married to Sigurd Guttormson d.e. Torsnes.
1 CONT 
1 CONT He was called a "noble farmer" which means he was upper class. He owned Norheim, Skutlaberg, and part of Nesthus. Based on who his daughters were married to, and how much land they owned, it is reasonable to count him in the aristocracy.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Guttorm's son Ivar inherited all of Norheim. His sons-in-law, Peter and Sigurd, split the remaining farms in Hardanger.
