0 @NFS673@ NOTE Chapter 3.    KINGS of DENMARK 1047-1412 (FAMILY of THORGILS)B.      KINGS of DENMARK 1047-14122.         ERIK (1216-murdered 10 Aug 1250, bur Schleswig St Peter, transferred 1257 to Ringsted Church).- - -m (Papal dispensation 4o Anagni 31 J
1 CONC ul 1239, 9 Oct 1239) as her first husband, JUTTA von Sachsen, daughter of ALBRECHT I Duke of Saxony & his first wife Anna of Austria.  The Chronica Jutensis records that "Ericum", son of "Waldemarus rex", married "Juttam filiam ducis Saxonie"[723]
1 CONC .  The Icelandic Annals record the marriage in 1239 of "Ericus Danorum rex Valdemari filius" and "Juttam filiam Henrici ducis Anhaltini"[724].  Pope Gregory IX issued a dispensation for the marriage of "Ericum filium Waldemari regis" and "Juttam fi
1 CONC liam ducis Saxoniæ" dated 31 Jul 1239[725].  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Iuttam [uxor] Ericus rex Dacie" as daughter of "Albertus dux" & his first wife Agnes[726].  The Annales Stadenses records the marriage "1239 die Dyonisii" of "Ericu
1 CONC s rex Daciæ [frater Abel]" and "filiam ducis Alberti de Anehalt"[727].  The Annales Ryenses record the marriage in 1239 of "rex Ericus" and "Iudith filiam ducis Saxoniæ"[728].  1250.  She married secondly Burchard von Querfurt-Magdeburg.  The pri
1 CONC mary source which confirms her second marriage has not yet been identified.King Erik IV & his wife had six children:- - -d)         INGEBORG ([1244]-24/26 Mar 1287).  The Icelandic Annals record the marriage in 1261 of "Rex Magnus" and "Ingeborga
1 CONC m filiam sancti Erici Valdemari filii Danorum regis"[730].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1287 of "Regina Ingeburga Erici filia"[731].  m (Bergen 11 Sep 1261) MAGNUS of Norway, son of HAAKON "den Gamle/the Old" King of Norway & his wif
1 CONC e Margret Skulesdatter (Tønsberg 1 May 1238-Bergen 9 May 1280, bur Bergen, St Olav's Abbey).  He succeeded his father in 1263 as MAGNUS IV "Lagabøte/Lagabæter/the Law-reformer" King of Norway.
