0 @NFS742@ NOTE Sigrid the Fair, died in 1289 and was buried in Skänninge Dominican monastery, was married to the lawman in Östergötland, Bengt Magnusson (died around 1294).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sigrid is known to posterity through the romantic late medieval legend of the battle between Bengt lagman and earl Birger, in which the earl is said to have been disarmed by Sigrid's beauty and wisdom. In fact, Sigrid and Bengt Magnusson married lo
1 CONC ng after Earl Birger had passed away. The legend is also known through Frans Hedberg's The Wedding at Ulvåsa from 1865.
0 @NFS743@ NOTE "Enligt Margareta Klausdotters bekanta, delvis rent ohistoriska berättelse var »Sigrid den fagra» av lägre börd än mannen."
