1 CONT Judith: This name has Hebrew origins and means "woman of Judea" or "praised." IN SWEDISH AND DANISH JUDITH = JUTTA
1 CONT 
1 CONT Albertsdotter: A patronymic surname meaning "daughter of Albert." In Scandinavian naming traditions, "dotter" means "daughter."
1 CONT 
1 CONT Askanier: This refers to the House of Ascania, a noble family from medieval Germany. The name is linked to Aschersleben, a town in Saxony-Anhalt, Germany.
1 CONT 
1 CONT So, in English, her name could be interpreted as Judith, daughter of Albert, of the House of Ascania
