0 @NFS883@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Ragna Erlingsdatter emerged in the mid‑12th century as the daughter of Erling Vidkunson Bjarkøy and Ragnhild Lodmundsdatter, members of the early Bjarkøy lineage rooted in northern Norway. Born around 1155—later associated with Bergen in mode
1 CONC rn records—she grew up in a period when Norway’s regional families were consolidating land, influence, and alliances through marriage.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Her life took a decisive turn when she married Lagmann Bjarne Mårdsøn Bjarkøy in 1179, a union that strengthened the Bjarkøy family's standing in Troms. Together they had at least two children, including Ivar Bjarnesson Bjarkøy. Ragna’s impo
1 CONC rtance in the lineage became especially clear after the early death of her brother Vidkun in 1182. With the male line extinguished, Ragna became the bearer of the family’s continuity—the younger Bjarkøy-ætten flowed through her descendants.
1 CONT 
1 CONT She lived into the 1230s, passing away in Bjarkøy Parish in 1235. Though the surviving records are sparse and largely unsourced, her role as the matriarch who carried forward a prominent northern Norwegian family places her among the quiet but ess
1 CONC ential figures who shaped medieval regional dynasties.
