0 @NFS941@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT GOOGLE TRANSLATE:
1 CONT Gaut or Gaute på Ænes is said to have been of an old squire's family, and was himself a squire under King Magnus Erlingsson in the 1160s. The Norwegian title lendmann roughly corresponds to the French baron title, which later also found its way i
1 CONC nto Norway.
1 CONT He bid on Ænes in Kvinnherad and owned a lot of land, not only in Sunnhordland and Hardanger, but also elsewhere.
1 CONT We do not know much more about Gaut. But he had two sons, Jon and Munan, about whom we know little more. They were also squires and took part in the battles against King Sverre. After Sverre's victory, however, it seems that they have reached a set
1 CONC tlement with him. This allowed them to keep their properties and rights.
1 CONT Odd Handegård discusses the claim that Gaut came from Ænes in our family history, and in this connection refers to an article by Hallvard Magerøy: "Urnes stavkyrkje, Ornes-ætta og Ornes-godset" (Historisk Tidsskrift 2/88), where it is argued be
1 CONC cause Gaut came from Ornes in Sogn and not from Ænes in Kvinnherad, as had been claimed since the historian P.A. Munch.
1 CONT 
1 CONT I dispute the claim made by Munch because GAUTE was buried at Ænes Kirkegård, Kvinnherad, Hordaland, Norway.
1 CONT MARCIA LEE
