0 @NFS1318@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Cecilia Knutsdotter (Aspenäsätten) 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Cecilia Knutsdotter , died sometime after March 12, 1350, was a Swedish landowner. She was the daughter of the governor and councilor Knut Jonsson (Aspenäsätten) . She was married to Bo Nilsson (Night and Day) . They are both mentioned as betroth
1 CONC ed on May 16, 1306. On March 25, 1336, as a widow, she donates, with the consent of her children, a farm in Torpa sn to St. Martin's monastery in Skänninge , in whose monastery her daughter Elena Bosdotter joined in 1336. She also owned land in Br
1 CONC åbo and Ydre hd in Östergötland.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bo Bosson (Night and Day) , National Councillor.
1 CONT Elena Bosdotter
1 CONT See also 
1 CONT The aspen ridges ^ Leo van de Pas, Genealogics , 2003, read online and read online . [source from Wikidata]
