0 @NFS1561@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT "Jon Hafthorsson. Gjorde jämte brodern Sigurd Hafthorson och andra uppror mot konung Magnus Eriksson 1333, men detta stillades snart. Deltog 1337 ånyo i en uppresning mot konungen, varunder Akershus intogs, men förlikning slöts 1339-08-15 i Boh
1 CONC us. Var riddare och riksråd 1343, då de norska stormännen hyllade Håkan Magnusson som konung i Norge. Fråndömdes 1347 jämte brodern Sigurd Borgesyssels län i Smaalenenes amt, som bröderna erhållit i förläning av morfadern, konung Håkan
1 CONC . Undertecknade konung Magnus' norska testamente 1349. Sålde 1350-02-21 sin hälft i Hammarö i Värmland, som han erhållit med sin hustru, till konung Magnus. Deltog i mötet i Bohus 1361, då det norska riksrådet anslöt sig till Sveriges för
1 CONC bund med hansestäderna. Kallas baro regni Norvegiæ 1369. Satt i riksrådet ännu 1380. Bodde på sina egendomar Huseby på halvön Onsö i Borgesyssel och Ellingård i Smaalenene. Levde ännu 1395 [N. F. och RKn]. Gift före 1350 med Birgitta Knu
1 CONC tsdotter, död 1395 på Huseby, dotter av lagmannen, först i Värmland, sedan i Västergötland, riddaren och riksrådet Knut Magnusson (lejon, Tyrgils Knutssons ätt) och Cecilia Röriksdotter (griphuvud, Algotsönernas ätt)."
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Jon Hafthorsson. Together with his brother Sigurd Hafthorson and others rebelled against King Magnus Eriksson in 1333, but this was soon put down. In 1337 he again participated in an uprising against the king, during which Akershus was captured, b
1 CONC ut a settlement was concluded on 1339-08-15 in Bohus. Was a knight and riksråd 1343, when the Norwegian nobles hailed Håkan Magnusson as king of Norway. Condemned in 1347 together with his brother Sigurd Borgesyssel's county in Smaalenenes county
1 CONC , which the brothers received as a fief from their maternal grandfather, King Håkan. Signed King Magnus' Norwegian will in 1349. Sold 1350-02- 21 his half in Hammarö in Värmland, which he obtained with his wife, to King Magnus. Participated in t
1 CONC he meeting in Bohus in 1361, when the Norwegian Riksad joined Sweden's confederation with the Hanseatic cities. Called baro regni Norvegiæ in 1369. Sat in the Riksad until 1380. Lived on his estates Huseby on the peninsula Onsö in Borgesyssel an
1 CONC d Ellingård in Smaalenene. Still alive in 1395 [N. F. and RKn]. Married before 1350 to Birgitta Knutsdotter, died 1395 at Huseby, daughter of lawman nen, first in Värmland, then in Västergötland, the knight and councilor Knut Magnusson (lion, T
1 CONC yrgils Knutsson's family) and Cecilia Röriksdotter (grip-head, Algotson's family)."
1 CONT 
1 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Roos_af_Hjelms%C3%A4ter_nr_51#TAB_1
