0 @NFS1615@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT ? Birgitta Jonsdotter. Was on 10.8 1325 long married to the Riksdag knight Peter Ragvaldsson (three boxes), who first appears in the sources in 1296 and was still alive in 1326. Since the spouses on the above-mentioned day call the Duke Knut Jonsso
1 CONC n (tab. 3) »gener et cognatus», it has been assumed , that she was his sister. However, one cannot rule out the possibility that Birgitta was the daughter of Johan Birgersson, who in a 1310 authenticated letter without specified date is said to h
1 CONC ave mortgaged 2 örtugland of land in Österröra village in Västra Ryds sn in Bro hd in Uppland to Uppsala Cathedral. In the same village, the husband and wife of the couple also mortgaged in 1322 16 örtugland, belonging to Peter Ragvaldsson, t
1 CONC o Uppsala Cathedral, with his consent, and in 1325 Peter Ragvaldsson and his wife Drotsen Knut Jonsson authorized at the ting to announce their bequest of 1 markland of land in Österröra to the same cathedral building fund. If one assumes with th
1 CONC e support of this that Birgitta was the daughter of Johan Birgersson, he may have been the son of Birger Filipsson (tab. 1), but before he married Ulfhild Magnusdotter. In addition to patronymics and the spouses' kinship with Knut Jonsson, the foll
1 CONC owing property holdings could speak for this. In 1279, Birger donated a nearby farm Tibble to Fogdö monastery, which however was not allowed to possess the farm in peace. Birgitta also owned land in a Tibble, the location of which is not specifie
1 CONC d in the source either. A presumption that it would be the same Tibble that Birger owned is close at hand. Birgitta was the widow of Peter Ragvaldsson 31.5 1328, when she issued a letter at Nynäs in Bälinge sn in Rönö hd in Södermanland, and w
1 CONC as dead 1.8 1346. Owned mills in Torshälla in Södermanland, which she had exchanged for land in Närke, probably in Grimstens hd. It is likely that the lion eagle coat of arms mentioned in the introduction on Sten Bielke's canvas belongs to Birgi
1 CONC tta's family, because this coat of arms, among other combinations, is presented three times in the drawing next to another, which represents three red bars arranged in a field of gold, apparently her husband's coat of arms.
0 @NFS1616@ NOTE 
