0 @NFS1736@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT He was a knight ("væpner") and riksråd (minister?). 
1 CONT 
1 CONT In the town of Tønsberg, county Vestfold, he was the exchequer or "fehirde". A "fehirde" was a term used in the Norwegian middle ages, equaliant to a "tax minister" or "royal treasurer". Under the rule of Haakon V of Norway in the early 14th centu
1 CONC ry, the country was divided into five "fehirdsler" (=tax districts).
