0 @NFS1871@ NOTE Barn
1 CONT Johan Magnusson, knight and lawman, was the son of Magnus Gregersson.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Gregers Magnusson was forced to spend many years in exile in Denmark after falling out of favor with King Magnus Eriksson . He probably fell around 1348 during King Magnus' First Crusade against the Republic of Novgorod . A fate that also befell hi
1 CONC s brothers Johan Magnusson and Karl Magnusson .
1 CONT In 1378 Johan Magnusson's daughter Ingegärd seals a gift deed together with her husband Henrik Reventlow and the witnesses Magnus Trottesson, Johan Trottesson, Lars Björnsson and Tideke Pinnow . https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bj%C3%A4lbo%C3%A4tten
1 CONC s_o%C3%A4kta_gren
0 @NFS1872@ NOTE The illegitimate branch of the Folkunga family
1 CONT TABLE 11
1 CONT Johan Magnusson (son of Magnus Gregersson, tab. 3). Mentioned for the first time in 1328. Was lawman (underlawman?) in Västmanland in 1335. Knighted sometime between 1335 and 1337, probably at the coronation of King Magnus 21.7 1336. Mentioned fo
1 CONC r the last time 4.9 1340. Owned Benhammar, now Benhamra, in Vada sn in Vallentuna hd in Uppland after maternal uncle Jedvard Filipsson ( Rumbyätten )
1 CONT 
1 CONT Daughter:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ingegärd Johansdotter. Mentioned as a widow at Benhammar 1365-1390. Donated with his daughter land in Bro hd in Uppland to St. Klara monastery. Was first married to king Magnus justitiarius and council knight Trotte Petersson ( Ekaätten ), who i
1 CONC s first mentioned in 1333 and was still alive in 1362 but probably died in 1363. Mrs. Ingegärd was remarried in 1367 to the knight Henrik Reventlow , who was still alive in 1382 but died in 1390.
