0 @NFS2154@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT ISABEL DE BRUCE (ISABEL BRUCE) IS NOT THE SAME AS ISABELLA OF MAR
1 CONT Isabel de Bruce was the daughter of Robert de Brus, 6th Lord of Annandale and Marjorie, Countess of Carrick. She was born in 1272 at Turnberry Castle in Carrick, Scotland. Isabel had many siblings including older half sister Martha Kilconquhar an
1 CONC d younger brothers Robert the Bruce, King of Scots, and Edward Bruce, High King of Ireland. 
1 CONT In 1293 at the age of 21, Isabel married King Eric II of Norway, becoming his 2nd wife and Queen Consort of Norway.
1 CONT Eric and Isabel had one child, a daughter, Ingeborg Eriksdottir born on 1297. 
1 CONT Eric II, died on 15 July 1299, without male heirs and was succeeded by his younger brother, Haakon V. 
1 CONT Dowager Queen Isabel did not return to Scotland but continued to live at court in Bergen, Norway. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Isabel betrothed her 3 year old daughter Ingeborg to Jon Magnusson, Earl of Orkney in 1300 but the marriage never took place, Ingeborg instead married Valdemar Magnusson of Sweden, Duke of Finland, in 1312.
1 CONT Isabel herself remained a widow and never remarried. Her daughter Ingeborg died in 1357 and Isabel died in 1358 in Bergen, Norway.
