0 @NFS2243@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Margrete Tordsdatter Agaten was born around 1295 in the rural parish landscape of Aker, Oslo, during a period when the farms surrounding medieval Oslo formed tight-knit kin networks. She was the daughter of Tord Erlingssen Bonde and Ragna Olavsdatt
1 CONC er på Stein, families rooted in the agricultural nobility that managed land, labor, and local obligations in the Oslo region.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sometime around 1320, Margrete married Torgeir Audunsson Hnater, a union that linked two established farm families and strengthened their standing within the community. They lived at Agaten, søndre Bjølsen, a farm cluster north of medieval Oslo
1 CONC , where Margrete spent her adult life managing household responsibilities, seasonal labor, and the social obligations expected of a landholding woman in early 14th‑century Norway.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Margrete and Torgeir had at least one known child, Olav Torgeirsson Bjølsen, born in 1339. Her life unfolded during a turbulent era marked by shifting political power and the early pressures that would precede the mid‑century plague. She died i
1 CONC n 1352 at Agaten, remembered within her family line as part of the foundational generation that anchored the Bjølsen–Aker kin network.
