0 @NFS2340@ NOTE Summary: 
1 CONT Gulathingslagmand  Baaard Peterssön frikjender ifølge et irettelagt Prov Olav Karl (i Hardanger) for Brødrene Romunds og Ottars tiltale angaaende deres moders død.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [google translations, rough]
1 CONT Gulathingslagmand Baaard Peterssön acquits Olav Karl (in Hardanger) of the charges of Brødrene Romunds and Ottar regarding the death of their mother, according to an organized trial.
1 CONT 
1 CONT NB: ‘Sigurd a Thorsnese’ sealed a letter as a member of the jury that judged this case when it was tried; Bård Pedersen seems to be confirming their acquittal.
0 @NFS2341@ NOTE Summary: Sigurd Guttormsen serves as witness to the sale of Steinsland & Gerde by Guttorm Jonsen on behalf of Hr. Finn Ogmundsen to Torgeir Tovesen
0 @NFS2342@ NOTE Summary:
1 CONT Ivar Guttormsön skifter Fædrenearven med sine Svogre Peter og Sigurd, der paa sine Hustruers Vegne erholde forskjellige Gaarde i Hardanger imod Gaarden Norheim m.m., som var Ivar fik uskiftet.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [google translation, rough]
1 CONT Ivar Guttormsön shifts his father's inheritance with his brothers-in-law Peter and Sigurd, who on behalf of their wives receive various farms in Hardanger against the farms in Norheim, etc., which Ivar got unshifted.
0 @NFS2343@ NOTE Summary:
1 CONT Kong Magnus befaler Ivar Lagmand at indstævne for sig Svein paa Stein og Peter paa Sandvin og dømme dem mellem i en Trætte om to Nøsttofter paa Sandvin.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [google translation, rough]
1 CONT King Magnus orders Ivar Lagmand to sue for himself Svein on Stein and Peter on Sandvin and judge them in a Trätte for two Nøsttofter [boathouses] on Sandvin. [mentions Sigurd Galte (Sigur∂r galta), Tores Gautsen (Gauz sona), Øystein Bårdsen (
1 CONC OEystæns Bærdors sonar)....lagretmenn in the boathouse case]
0 @NFS2344@ NOTE Summary:
1 CONT Eirik Abbed i Halsnø, Broder Aslak, Ingeborg paa Skjalnes, Peter paa Sandvin, Gudleik i Huggul, Sigurd paa Thorsnes og Jon paa Norheim værdsætte det Gods, som Thorkel Bonde udbetalte sin Sønnekone Ingegerd.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [google translation, rough]
1 CONT Eirik the Abbot of Halsnø, Brother Aslak, Ingeborg of Skjalnes, Peter of Sandvin, Gudleik of Huggul, Sigurd of Thorsnes and Jon of Norheim value the Estate that Thorkel the Farmer paid his son's wife Ingegerd.
0 @NFS2345@ NOTE Summary:
1 CONT 5 menn kunngjør vitnesbyrd som Peter på Sandven lot føre fram om ei nausttuft som Svein på Steine gjorde krav på. Peter hadde krevd at bade det naustet som stod på tufta, og båtene som var oppsatt der, skulle fjernes innen 5 dager.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [google translation, rough]
1 CONT 5 men announce testimony that Peter på Sandven brought forward about a naustuft that Svein på Steine claimed. Peter had demanded that the boathouse that stood on the ground, and the boats that were set up there, be removed within 5 days.
0 @NFS2346@ NOTE Torleiv prestsson, lensmann for herr Arne i Hardanger, kunngjør vitnesbyrd om et naust og ei nausttuft på Sandven (i Kvam). Jfr. nr. 16 og 17 her nedenfor, og DN XI nr. 7 og I nr. 166.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [google translation, rough]
1 CONT Torleiv prestsson, sheriff for Mr. Arne in Hardanger, announces testimony [some provided by Sigurd Torsnes] about a boathouse and a boathouse at Sandven (in Kvam). Cf. no. 16 and 17 here below, and DN XI no. 7 and I no. 166.
0 @NFS2347@ NOTE Summary:
1 CONT Sigurd Galte og Torleiv Erlingsson kunngjør en avtale mellom Asbjørn Sigurdsson og hans måg Sigurd om et arveskifte etter Sigurd på Fet og hans hustru Arnbjørg. Asbjørn opptrådte på vegne av seg selv, sin bror Isak og sine søstre Rannvei
1 CONC g og Ragnhild, Sigurd på vegne av seg selv og sin hustru Margareta. [then details who inherits what of the estate]
1 CONT 
1 CONT [google translation, rough]
1 CONT Sigurd Galte and Torleiv Erlingsson announce an agreement between Asbjørn Sigurdsson and his brother-in-law Sigurd about an inheritance after Sigurd på Fet and his wife Arnbjørg. Asbjørn appeared on behalf of himself, his brother Isak and his s
1 CONC isters Rannveig and Ragnhild, Sigurd on behalf of himself and his wife Margareta.
0 @NFS2348@ NOTE 2 menn (i Hardanger) utsteder vitnemål om delesgang mellom Kalvanes og Dritvik foretatt av Sigurd på Torsnes, på vegne av sin bror Nikolas, Sigurd på Øystese, på egne vegne, og 5 andre menn. Grensene angis.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [google translation, rough]
1 CONT 2 men (in Hardanger) issue certificates of delesgang [the survey?] between Kalvanes and Dritvik made by Sigurd på Torsnes, on behalf of his brother Nikolas, Sigurd på Øystese, on his own behalf, and 5 other men. The boundaries are specified.
0 @NFS2349@ NOTE Confirms Bård og Guttorm Sigurdsen’s timber rights at Knarrevik forest (Ornes/Ænes parish), and confirms their right through descent from Viking på Torsnes through 6 generations: 
1 CONT “[To] All men who see or hear this letter send Viking Eirikson, Aslak Torkelson, Ketil Erlandson, Viking Gudleikson, Gunnar Askjellson and Tore Sigurdson, noblemen of God and theirs, greetings, as they make it known that we know to be true what o
1 CONC ur fathers told us and likewise the oldest men who lived in Varaldsøy skiprede and Jondal parish, and have heard nothing else, except that the Torsnesmen, one after the other who are mentioned here: Viking [‘the Rich’] and Inga, his daughter
1 CONC , Guttorm Kalvson (her son) and Sigurd Guttormson, Guttorm Sigurdson, Sigurd Guttormson, Bård and Guttorm Sigurdsønner, own and have owned the Knarrevik forest out to the gorge at Årsand and into Årvik ... between mountain and fjord as eterna
1 CONC l property, one after the other as we have mentioned before. We the aforesaid courtiers have never heard of herding or mentioned that the Torsnesmenne gave (“guldo”) or sold to anyone, but that each, one after the other, has inherited the afore
1 CONC mentioned forest Knarrevik, which is located in the parish of Ænes and Varaldsøy skiprede in Sunnhordland, and in true testimony of this we put our seals to this letter which was set up on Thursday the first day of summer in the 20th year of th
1 CONC e reign of our lord Eirik with God’s grace Norway king”.
