0 @NFS2441@ NOTE 
0 @NFS2442@ NOTE Tab 4
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ulf Abjörnsson (son of Abjörn Sixtensson, tab. 2). Appears in the records from 1317. Became a knight some of the years 1322—1325, possibly at the Täljemötet in June 1322. Mentioned as a councilor from 1320 and as a lawyer in Tiohärad 1347. D
1 CONC ied 1347 or 1348. About him are two of St. Birgitta's revelations. Married for the first time no later than 1317 to Kristina, who was still alive in 1326 but probably died in 1330, daughter of Councilor Sigmund Keldorsson and his wife Cecilia, an
1 CONC d the second time not later than 1337 to Märta, who was still alive in 1362 but died in 1381 and lived at Fågelvik in Tryserums sn in Norra Tjusts hd in Småland, daughter of the ten-district lawyer the knight Sune Jonsson ( Bååt ) and Katarin
1 CONC a Glysingsdotter ( Glysing ).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT 1. Karl Ulfsson, 1349, died 1407, knight, councilor, lawman, marshal. See tab. 5.
1 CONT Filip Ulfsson. Died no later than 1349.
1 CONT 2. Ingeborg. Died no later than 1362. Owned land in Hammarkinds hd in Östergötland. Married no later than 1352 to later Duke Bengt Algotsson, who displaced her and was killed around 1360. - Ingeborg died childless and inherited by her mother an
1 CONC d full sister.
1 CONT 2. Kristina. Buried in Vadstena monastery 30.8 1389. Her manor was after modern Fågelvik. Married for the first time in 1360 to Magister Nils Jonsson ( Rickebyätten ), who was councilor and lawyer in Östergötland in 1364 and probably died som
1 CONC e of the years 1364—1366, and second time to councilor Peter Ribbing , who died in Florence in 1379. Kristina died childless and inherited by half-brother Karl, who made large donations for her soul reputation.
