0 @NFS2565@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Richeza of Sweden (Swedish: Rikissa Valdemarsdotter, Polish: Ryksa szwedzka, Ryksa Waldemarówna; between 1265 and 1270 – before 1292) was a Swedish princess member of the House of Bjälbo and by marriage Duchess of Greater Poland during 1285-129
1 CONC 2 and High Duchess consort of Poland during 1290-1291.
1 CONT 
1 CONT She was a daughter of Valdemar, King of Sweden and Sophia of Denmark, daughter of the King Eric IV.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Life
1 CONT Her exact date of birth is unknown, but is generally placed as the third daughter and fifth child born of her parents' marriage (at all, they had seven children, two sons and five daughters). She was certainly born before 1273, because by that yea
1 CONC r she and her sister Katharina were considered for possible marriage with Otto, only son and heir of John, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg.[1] However, the marriage negotiations ended without results.
