1 CONT Full text (in Icelandic): 
1 CONT Let Hakon, by the grace of God, the kings of Norway and Sweden, further declare with this letter that they are to pay off a debt owed to the merchant Tidike of Lyne. eleven marks of silver and fifteen English shillings and four marks of silver. Le
1 CONC t this debt be paid to Tideko, the agents of Bergen, Ellender Philippusson Joon Haluardzson. And Andres a Mork, of the goods that Andres has now brought to Norway, of Iceland, who are also to pay tribute and honor to them, that they may pay off th
1 CONC e debts of Tidiko, his agents, the said eleven marks of silver as much as he can, according to the goods he has brought to Bergen, as far as they will do what is right to us, we shall give to them as our agents. Ellend. Jon and Andres both agreed t
1 CONC o the terms of the aforementioned 18th century treaty, with a letter written at Tunsberg House on the day after Easter, stating that the kingdoms of Norway and our seafaring peoples were united.
