0 @NFS2607@ NOTE TAB 13
1 CONT Sten Turesson (son of Ture Bengtsson, Tab. 12), to Örby and Vik in Balingsta parish, both of which belonged to his mother's family, Ekholmen in Veckholm parish, which he received through his 1st marriage, both in Uppsala county, and from 1419 Foge
1 CONC lvik in Tryserum parish, Kalmar county. Was a gunsmith living on Ekholmen 1414. Riksråd no later than 1422. Hövidsman at Piksborg 1426-02-02. Died 1431 before 27/6 and buried 1431-09-08 in Vadstena. He was later King Karl Knutsson's guardian an
1 CONC d foster father. Married 1: o 1414 to Margareta Karlsdotter (sparre) in her 2nd marriage [married 1: o 1408 to the knight and captain of Åbo Knut Tordsson Bonde, died 1413 and in this married mother of King Karl Knutsson], died around 1428, daught
1 CONC er of the knight, councilor and marshal, the lawyer in Uppland Karl Ulfsson ( Sparre of Tofta ) to Tofta and Helena Israelsdotter ( Finstaätten ). Married 2nd probably 1429 with Agneta Eriksdotter Krummedige in her 1st marriage (married 2nd with A
1 CONC xel Nilsson to Barsebek), died (Bbl.) Between 1452-09-14 and 1453-06-01, daughter of the Danish Governor and Councilor Erik Krummedige to Tranekärr and his 1st wife Beata von Thienen . She owned Örby, which she sold in 1451 to her nephew Johan Kr
1 CONC istersson ( Vaasa ) (Bbl.).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT 1. Ture Stensson, born around 1416. Gunman. Riksråd 1436. Lagman in Uppland 1438-03-06 and also chief at Älvsborg in the beginning of 1439. Repulsed a Norwegian attack on this fortress in the summer of 1439. Then participated in the autumn of 143
1 CONC 9 in the lord's day in Telge (Bbl.), Where King Erik definitely deposed, and then accompanied his half-brother, the head of state Karl Knutsson on his journey to Kalmar, but fell ill quickly just south of Nyköping and died after a few days, probab
1 CONC ly (1439) 23/10 and buried 1439-10-29 in Vadstena (Bbl .).
1 CONT 1. Knut Stensson , to Ekholmen. Became a knight at King Kristoffer's coronation in 1441. Riksråd. Received at Karl Knutsson's accession to the throne Axvall Castle County, but soon exchanged this for Nyköping Castle and County (Bbl.). Lagman in U
1 CONC ppland 1450. Died 1451 and buried 1451-11-11 in Vadstena. Married [? 1st with Kerstin Knutsdotter , daughter of Knut Bengtsson (Blå) to Arnäs. Married 2nd] with Elin Gustafsdotter in her 1st marriage [married 2nd before 1455 with the knight and h
1 CONC ead of state Erik Axelsson (Tott), died just before 1481-03-28]. Lived 1494-07-15 but was dead 1496-06-02, daughter of the knight and councilor Gustaf Algotsson ( Sture ) to Ängsö and Lagmansö and his 2nd wife Märta Ullsdotter ( Sparre of Hjuls
1 CONC ta and Ängsö ).
1 CONT 1. Margareta Stensdotter , died 1439. Married no later than 1436 (Bbl.) To the Riksrådet and the captain at Stegeborg Nils Stensson ( Night and Day ), died 1439-10-00 in Norrköping (SK.).
1 CONT 1. Birgitta Stensdotter to Ekholmen after her brother Knut Stensson's death 1451 (Bbl.) Lived 1461-01-02 but was dead (Bbl.) 1464-06-04. Married 1st before 1438-08-29 with the knight, riksrådet and hövidsmannen at Kalmar castle Gustaf Anundsson S
1 CONC ture, died 1444 (Pt XXI p. 103.), and in this married mother of the head of state Sten Sture d. Ä. Married 2: o before 1446-12-02 with the knight, riksrådet and lagmannen in Uppland Gustaf Karlsson (gumsehuvud) to Ekholmen, in his 2nd marriage [m
1 CONC arried 1st with Märta Karlsdotter. Married 3: o 1474 to Ingeborg Filipsdotter, daughter of Filip Axelsson (Tott)], died 1486-07-26.
1 CONT 1. Katarina Stensdotter, to Vik, lived widow 1458. Married 1438-10-00 to the Danish knight and councilor Klaus Nilsson ( Sparre of Ellinge ), to Ellinge in Skåne, lived 1449, but died 1452-02.
1 CONT 2. Two sons and a daughter, dead young.
