0 @NFS2904@ NOTE Jon Hafthorsson . He rebelled against King Magnus Eriksson in 1333, together with his brother Sigurd Hafthorson and others, but this was soon put down. He participated in another uprising against the king in 1337, during which Akershus wa
1 CONC s captured, but a settlement was reached on 15 August 1339 in Bohus. He was a knight and a councillor in 1343, when the Norwegian nobles hailed Håkan Magnusson as king of Norway. He was deprived in 1347, together with his brother Sigurd, of the co
1 CONC unty of Borgesyssel in the county of Smaalene, which the brothers had received as a grant from their grandfather, King Håkan. He signed King Magnus' Norwegian will in 1349. He sold his half in Hammarö in Värmland, which he had received with hi
1 CONC s wife, to King Magnus on 21 February 1350. Participated in the meeting in Bohus in 1361, when the Norwegian royal council joined Sweden's alliance with the Hanseatic cities. Called baro regni Norvegiæ in 1369. Still sat in the royal council in 13
1 CONC 80. Lived on his estates Huseby on the Onsö peninsula in Borgesyssel and Ellingård in Smaalenene. Still alive in 1395 [NF and RKn]. Married before 1350 to Birgitta Knutsdotter, died in 1395 at Huseby, daughter of the magistrate, first in Värmlan
1 CONC d, then in Västergötland, the knight and royal councilor Knut Magnusson (lion, Tyrgils Knutssons family ) and Cecilia Röriksdotter (griphead, Algotsönernas family ).
0 @NFS2905@ NOTE GEDCOM data
0 @NFS2906@ NOTE GEDCOM data
0 @NFS2907@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Adelsvapen.com (in sources)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ulf Philippusson (son of Philippus Ulfsson, tab. 3). Appears no earlier than 1319. Became a knight between 7.1 and 29.7 1333 and the latter date was one of the two governors in Skåne. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT His manor was Vinäs in Gammalkils sn, Valkebo hd in Östergötland. Married to a daughter of the knight, the Riksrådet and the lawyer in Södermanland Staffan Röriksson (through mantle cut 3 times divided shield). She died in 1349 and left lan
1 CONC d in Algutsrums hd on Öland and Norra Möre and Uppvidinge hd in Småland.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ingeborg Ulfsdotter. Owned land in Selebo hd in Södermanland, Simtuna hd in Uppland and Dals hd in Östergötland. Called "wife" after her death, although none of her wives were knights, which indicates that she became a nun as a widow, especiall
1 CONC y as her will is dated in Vårfruberga monastery and she wanted to be buried there. Died between 10.12 1393 and 25.1 1395. Received 3.7 1343 land in Tveta and Vista hd in Småland as a morning gift from Nils Hemmingsson (Lejonansikte), who is menti
1 CONC oned in life 1340-1344. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT 18.2 1356 she remarried to Magnus Nilsson (Revelstaätten) at Revelsta in Altuna sn, Simtuna hd in Uppland, which then as a morning gift gave her soil in this hd. As his widow, she is mentioned in 1360, when she was awarded one of her morning gift
1 CONC s from her first marriage, which Magnus pledged. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT 27.10 1362 she received land in Norra Vedbo and Tveta hd in Småland as a morning gift from Harald Kase , who appears 1343 - 27.6 1381, had been married before and also owned land in Gäsene hd in Västergötland and Simtuna hd in Uppland.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Magnus Ulfsson. Owned land in Bobergs hd in Östergötland and sealed 1354 with the wolf weapon. Possibly identical with the person with this name who in 1361 owned land in Hammarkinds hd in Östergötland (DS, no. 6461). Was dead 28.3 1379.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Staffan Ulfsson, 1357, begr. 1393, knight, district chief, bailiff, councilor. See tab. 5 .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Barnam Ulfsson, 1370, however 1378 or 1379. See tab. 8 .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ingrid Ulfsdotter. Owned land in Tjusts hd in Småland and was married to the citizen Jon Kogger in Vimmerby.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  ? Katarina Ulfsdotter. Owned land in the same place in Tjust as Ingrid Ulfsdotter.
