0 @NFS2984@ NOTE "Tures hustru hette Sigrid och överlevde honom. Enligt uppgift av den gamle genealogen Utter, som sett ett av henne beseglat, numera förlorat brev av år 1327, förde hon en sparre i vapnet; uppgiften kan möjligen anses bekräftad därav
1 CONC , att Tures söner bevisligen voro släkt med den från konung Magnus Erikssons tid bekante Ulf Abjörnsson (sparre)."
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Ture's wife's name was Sigrid and she survived him. According to information from the old genealogist Utter, who saw a letter sealed by her, now lost, from the year 1327, she carried a spar in her weapon; the information can possibly be considere
1 CONC d confirmed by this, that Ture's sons were demonstrably related to Ulf Abjörnsson (sparre) known from the time of King Magnus Eriksson."
1 CONT 
1 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=18188
0 @NFS2985@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT "Sigrid Nilsdotter. Förde en sparre i vapnet enligt uppgift hos Utter, vilket inte behöver vara ett misstag, utan hon kan ha upptagit sin moders vapen, gift med lagmannen i Värend Ture Kettilsson Bielke i hans 2:a gifte, känd 1283-1322, var dö
1 CONC d 1327. PhT:1958 s30f; SBL:26 s408"
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Sigrid Nilsdotter. Brought a spar in the coat of arms according to Utter, which need not be a mistake, but she may have taken up her mother's coat of arms, married to the lawman in Värend Ture Kettilsson Bielke in his 2nd marriage, known 1283-132
1 CONC 2, was dead in 1327. PhT:1958 p30f; SBL:26 p408"
1 CONT 
1 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Natt_och_Dag_nr_13#TAB_6
0 @NFS2986@ NOTE Approximate birthyear, Sigthora.
0 @NFS2987@ NOTE Ulf Philippusson (son of Philippus Ulfsson, tab. 3). Appears no earlier than 1319. Became a knight between 7.1 and 29.7 1333 and the latter date was one of the two governors in Skåne. His manor was Vinäs in Gammalkils sn, Valkebo hd in Ö
1 CONC stergötland. Married to a daughter of the knight, the Riksrådet and the lawyer in Södermanland Staffan Röriksson (through mantle cut 3 times divided shield). She died in 1349 and left land in Algutsrums hd on Öland and Norra Möre and Uppvidin
1 CONC ge hd in Småland.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ingeborg Ulfsdotter. Owned land in Selebo hd in Södermanland, Simtuna hd in Uppland and Dals hd in Östergötland. Called "wife" after her death, although none of her wives were knights, which indicates that she became a nun as a widow, especiall
1 CONC y as her will is dated in Vårfruberga monastery and she wanted to be buried there. Died between 10.12 1393 and 25.1 1395. Received 3.7 1343 land in Tveta and Vista hd in Småland as a morning gift from Nils Hemmingsson (Lejonansikte), who is menti
1 CONC oned in life 1340-1344. 18.2 1356 she remarried to Magnus Nilsson ( Revelstaätten) at Revelsta in Altuna sn, Simtuna hd in Uppland, which then as a morning gift gave her soil in this hd. As his widow, she is mentioned in 1360, when she was awarde
1 CONC d one of her morning gifts from her first marriage, which Magnus pledged. 27.10 1362 she received land in Norra Vedbo and Tveta hd in Småland as a morning gift from Harald Kase , who appears 1343 - 27.6 1381, had been married before and also owne
1 CONC d land in Gäsene hd in Västergötland and Simtuna hd in Uppland.
1 CONT Magnus Ulfsson. Owned land in Bobergs hd in Östergötland and sealed 1354 with the wolf weapon. Possibly identical with the person with this name who in 1361 owned land in Hammarkinds hd in Östergötland (DS, no. 6461). Was dead 28.3 1379.
1 CONT Staffan Ulfsson, 1357, begr. 1393, knight, district chief, bailiff, councilor. See tab. 5 .
1 CONT Barnam Ulfsson, 1370, however 1378 or 1379. See tab. 8 .
1 CONT Ingrid Ulfsdotter. Owned land in Tjusts hd in Småland and was married to the citizen Jon Kogger in Vimmerby.
1 CONT  ? Katarina Ulfsdotter. Owned land in the same place in Tjust as Ingrid Ulfsdotter.
