0 @NFS3083@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Herr Guttorm Eriksson, born 1280, died 1349. He is believed to be the son of Erik Hudfat, but this is not certain. He was Knight, Councilor and Governor in southern Gudbrandsdalen and mentioned as the owner of, among other things, Nesøen in Asker
1 CONC . Married to Mrs Elin Olavsdatter (1295-1349) Leistad has found that he was the first owner of Nesøya who is mentioned, but how he got Nesøya is not known. Whether he inherited the estate or received it as a reward from the king for having been o
1 CONC n the right side in the power struggle is not known. That such a prominent person is the owner confirms that the farm on Nesøya must have become a powerful factor in the centuries before. Nesøya was inherited by his daughter (Mrs.) Gudrun Olavsda
1 CONC tter (1320-1370) married 1 to Bergsvein Bårdsson (1315-1361) married 2 to Knight and Riksråd: Mr. Jon Toraldesson (1315-1370)
