0 @NFS3108@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Born in 1395 on Nesøya in Asker, Gudrun Olavsdatter grew up within a prominent landholding family tied to the estates of Nesøya and the wider noble networks of eastern Norway. She was the daughter of Olav Håkonsen Nesøya and Ingeborg Jonsdatte
1 CONC r Stjerne Borregård, families connected to both regional influence and longstanding farm-based identities.
1 CONT 
1 CONT As an adult, Gudrun’s life intersected with several noble houses. Across her lifetime she is associated with marriages or unions involving Erlend Eindridesson Losna, Hallvard Toraldesen, and Jon Svalesen Smør, reflecting the political and famili
1 CONC al alliances typical of medieval Norwegian aristocracy. Through these relationships she became the mother of children who continued the Losna and Holter lines, including Eindrid Erlandson Losna, Sigrid Erlandsdatter av Losna, and Gyrid Hallvardsdat
1 CONC ter Holter.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Her recorded alternate names—such as Gudrun Olavsdatter Kjællingmule, Gudrun Olavsdatter Bolt, and several patronymic spellings—show how later genealogists preserved different branches of her identity, linking her to multiple noble families an
1 CONC d farm estates.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Gudrun spent her final years in Losna, Sogn og Fjordane, where she died in 1475, leaving behind a legacy woven through several of Norway’s medieval noble families and preserved in both farm names and lineage traditions.
