0 @NFS3148@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Knutsson_(Bonde)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Karl Knutsson, oegentligt Karl VIII (riktigare vore Karl II, ett regentnummer som faktiskt användes i hans samtid[1]), född 1 oktober 1408 eller 1409, död 15 maj 1470, var svensk riksföreståndare 1438–1440, kung av Sverige 1448–1457, 1464
1 CONC –1465 och 1467–1470 samt som Karl I kung av Norge 1449–1450. Han var son till Knut Bonde och Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta). [...]
1 CONT 
1 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles(Karl)_VIII_of_Sweden
1 CONT 
1 CONT Charles (Karl)VIII of Sweden (1408 Uppsala - 1470 Stockholm, in reality Charles(Karl) II), Charles (Karl) I of Norway, also Carl (Karl), was king of Sweden (1448–1457, 1464–1465 and from 1467 to his death in 1470) and king of Norway (1449–145
1 CONC 0). [...]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Marriages and Children
1 CONT 
1 CONT With Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke):
1 CONT - Ture Karlsson (Bonde) (died young before 1447)
1 CONT - Christina Karlsdotter (Bonde) (ca 1432- before 1500), married 1446 to the noble, councillor, and courtier Erik Eriksson (Gyllenstierna)
1 CONT 
1 CONT With Catherine of Bjurum:
1 CONT - Margaret Karlsdotter (Bonde) (1442–1462)
1 CONT - Magdalena of Sweden (1445–1495), married to noble Ivar Axelsson (Tott) in 1466
1 CONT - Richeza Karlsdotter (Bonde) (born ca. 1445), *nun* at Vadstena Abbey
1 CONT - Bridget Karlsdotter (Bonde) (1446–1469), *nun* at Vadstena Abbey
1 CONT - four sons died early
1 CONT 
1 CONT With Kristina Abrahamsdotter:
1 CONT - Anna Karlsdotter (Bonde), married to the noble Håkan Svensson (Bölja), governor of Västerås castle.
1 CONT - Charles Bonde (Karlsson) (1465–1488)
1 CONT 
1 CONT He left only one young son, born of his mistress, Kristina Abrahamsdotter, whom he married on his deathbed. Though she was recognized as Queen, the Swedish government did not allow the boy, suddenly legitimized as Prince Charles (Karl Karlsson) t
1 CONC o succeed him, but appointed one of their number, Sten Sture the Elder (who was Charles's nephew) as regent. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT .
