0 @NFS3192@ NOTE Karl Knutsson, King Karl VIII Knutson (son of Knut Bonde, Tab. 6 ), born probably 1408, died 1470-05-15. King of Sweden 1448-06-20. Elected king of Norway in 1449. Lost his Norwegian crown as early as 1450. Deposed as king of Sweden in 1457
1 CONC , recalled as king in the autumn of 1464. Resigned the crown in 1465. Recalled king 1467-09. Married 1: o 1429-02-28 on Ekholmen to Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke) , daughter of the knight and councilor Ture Stensson ( Bielke ) and Birgitta Abrahamsd
1 CONC otter (bull head). Married 2: o 1438-10-05 in Stockholm to Katarina Karlsdotter (gumsehuvud) , daughter of riksrådet Karl Ormsson ( gumsehuvud ) and Märta Gregersdotter (Aspenäsätten ). Married 3: o 1470 with his wife Kristina Abrahamsdotte
1 CONC r , possibly the daughter of the district chief in Raseborg's western district Abraham Pedersson (half animal).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children: married 1st with Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke):
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ture Karlsson, died young before 1447-06-23.
1 CONT Kristina Karlsdotter, lived 1492-06-11. Married 1446-09-27 on Svartsjö to the knight and councilor, King Karl's courtier and the lawyer in Tiohärad Erik Eriksson ( Gyllenstierna ).
1 CONT Children: married 2nd with Katarina Karlsdotter (gumsehuvud):
1 CONT 
1 CONT Margareta Karlsdotter, died before 1465.
1 CONT Magdalena Karlsdotter, born around 1445, died 1495. Married 1466-09-21 in Nyköping to the knight and councilor, the captain of Visborg Ivar Axelsson ( Tott ).
1 CONT Birgitta Karlsdotter, born 1446, died in Vadstena monastery 1469-04-14. Nun
1 CONT Children: married 3rd with Kristina Abrahamsdotter:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Karl Karlsson. In the father's will in 1470, he was granted full inheritance rights and received on his lot, among other things, Rönö estate, Östergötland County, of which he should never have come into possession. Seems to have lived still 148
1 CONC 8-09-24. According to a 16th century account, he must have "lived and aged in a low and despised position" due to the fact that his true birth was not recognized after all.
