1 CONT Ulf Jonsson , (son of Jon Hafthorsson, table 1). Already in 1369 was a knight and King Håkan's councillor. The king's chieftain at Dal around 1370–1380 and at the same time district chief at Dal in 1378. Was still a Norwegian councilor in 1388
1 CONC , when Margareta was elected Norway's »wife and husband and full guardian» on 1388-03-02, but seems to have subsequently moved to Sweden, was he during Queen Margareta's time lived on his farm Ervalla in Ervalla parish, Örebro County, which he t
1 CONC ogether with Säby (Säbylund) in Kumla Parish, Örebro County, Vreta and Fånö in Löts Parish, Uppsala County as well as farms in Västmanland, Södermanland, Östergötland and Småland inherited from mother. Also owned his father's estate in N
1 CONC orway and inherited with his wife a number of farms in Östergötland and Värmland. Buried 1415-02-03 in Vadstena monastery. Inheritance was carried out on 1415-08-10 after him and his wife Märta. [RKn.]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Peter Ulfsson. National Council. See Tab. 3.
1 CONT Birgitta Ulfsdotter, inheritance after her was held in 1443. (Ss.) Married before 1415 to the bailiff of Västmanland, Bergslagen and Dalarne as well as the chieftain at Västerås castle, the squire Jösse Eriksson (Lykke), beheaded on 12/09/1436.
1 CONT Katarina Ulfsdotter , buried in 1415 in Vadstena monastery. Married to the knight Tord Bonde , died in 1412.
