0 @NFS3272@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Copied from Geni
1 CONT 
1 CONT Wilhelmine Brandt: Slægten Benkestok. Utgave Damms Antikvariat A.S, Oslo 1997: Side 5. (V. 1.-V. 9) V. 3) Trond Benkestok til Melø, død 1626 paa Sanct Andreæ Dag (30/11), begravet i Melø Kirke Adventssøndag s A.
1 CONT 
1 CONT I 1620 udstedte "Troen Benchestock et pandte bref til Niels Povelsøn paa en Vog Fiskes Leye i Beyeren".
1 CONT 
1 CONT Han har maaske været den mest fremtrædende af Brødrene og rimeligvis mere velstaaende end nogen af de andre.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Medens man fortiden ikke med Sikkerhed kan forfølge disses Efterslægt, kjendes derimot Trond Benkestoks Decendenter (gjennom hans datter Ermegaard) lige til Nutiden, og Melø Gaard vedblev i lange Tider at tilhøre denne Gren af Familj.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Gift med "Gjertrud Peitersdatter", der 21. juni 1628 holdt Jorde-skifte og Husbytte med Svogeren Johan Benkestok. Hun var maaske en Søster af Christopher Benkestoks Hustru Berete Pedersdatter.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT http://www.benkestok-ringen.no/
1 CONT 
1 CONT Reiste utenlands i 1599(i følge Asbjørn Hegge).
1 CONT 
1 CONT GEDCOM Source
1 CONT 
1 CONT @R450842596@ Ancestry Family Trees Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com. Original data: Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members.
1 CONT 
1 CONT GEDCOM Source
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ancestry Family Tree http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=115559719&pi...
1 CONT 
1 CONT GEDCOM Source
1 CONT 
1 CONT @R450842596@ Ancestry Family Trees Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com. Original data: Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members.
1 CONT 
1 CONT GEDCOM Source
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ancestry Family Tree http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=115559719&pi...
1 CONT 
1 CONT English Translation of Norwegian 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Wilhelmine Brandt: The Benkestok clan.  Edition Damms Antikvariat A.S, Oslo 1997: Page 5. (V. 1.-V. 9) V. 3) Trond Benkestok to Melø, died 1626 on Sanct Andreæ Dag (30/11), buried in Melø Church Adventssøndag s A.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  In 1620, "Troen Benchestock issued a pledged letter to Niels Povelsøn on a Vog Fiskes Leye in Beyeren".
1 CONT 
1 CONT  He has perhaps been the most prominent of the Brothers and reasonably more prosperous than any of the others.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  While the past cannot be traced with certainty to their Efterslægt, on the other hand, Trond Benkestok's descendants (through his daughter Ermegaard) are known right up to the present, and Melø Gaard continued to belong to this branch of the fam
1 CONC ily for a long time.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Married to "Gjertrud Peitersdatter", where on 21 June 1628 held a Land Exchange and House Exchange with Brother-in-Law Johan Benkestok.  She was perhaps a sister of Christopher Benkestok's wife Berete Pedersdatter.
