0 @NFS3300@ NOTE Deleted posted death in United States.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Death in the USA unlikely in the1500 or the 1600s.  Columbus did not get to the West Indies until 1492.  Norwegian immigration to the US started about 1825.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The Vikings were in Greenland and perhaps eastern North America in about 1000. But they did not stay.
1 CONT 
1 CONT There is a mention in one of the notes that Niels traveled abroad in 1599.  That means to travel to continental Europe. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jamestown founded 1607
1 CONT Pilgrams arrived 1620
1 CONT Philadelphia founded 1682
1 CONT Norwegian immigration started about 1825.
0 @NFS3301@ NOTE Nevnt means "mentioned".
1 CONT 
1 CONT Not sure what that means in the tab Naturalization. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT And why is there a post in Naturalization?  Where was he Naturalized and why??
1 CONT 
1 CONT He lived in Norway and may have traveled to the continental Europe, but Naturalization probably did not exist.  He did not go to the USA.
