0 @NFS3365@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Copied from Geni
1 CONT 
1 CONT Anne Benkestok, levde i 1599 ved Faderens Skifte. Wilhelmine Brandt, Slægten Benkestok.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Muligens gift med Ulrik Meier i Fana som hun fikk et barn med i 1599. [Jens Christensen lesemesters dagbok.]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jon Benkestoks datter Anna. Anna sin mor giftet seg på nytt før 1599 med Jens Christenssøn, lesemester i Bergen og senere prest i Nordfjordeid 1603-1611. De må ha blitt gift etter 3. nov. 1593, da hans første hustru, Elisabeth, døde. I sine o
1 CONC pptegnelser skriver jens at "XVI Septem Anno Domini 1599 bleff Anna Benckestock forløst paa Phana (Fana) met en Vng Søn ved Vlrich Meyer." Siden Anna Jonsdatter Benkestok var steddatter av Jens Christenssøn, er det rimelig å tro at det er hun s
1 CONC om nevnes her. Kåre sin konklusjon: Dette gjør at det er lite trolig at Anne Jonsdatter på Tjøtta er identisk med Anna Jonsdatter Benkestok.
1 CONT 
1 CONT GEDCOM Source
1 CONT 
1 CONT @R450842596@ Ancestry Family Trees Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com. Original data: Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members.
1 CONT 
1 CONT GEDCOM Source
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ancestry Family Tree http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=115559719&pi...
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT English Translation of above Norwegian 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Anne Benkestok, lived in 1599 at Faderens Skifte.  Wilhelmine Brandt, Clan Benkestok.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Possibly married to Ulrik Meier in Fana with whom she had a child in 1599. [Jens Christensen reading teacher's diary.]
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Jon Benkestok's daughter Anna.  Anna's mother remarried before 1599 to Jens Christenssøn, reading teacher in Bergen and later priest in Nordfjordeid 1603-1611.  They must have been married after 3 Nov.  1593, when his first wife, Elisabeth, died
1 CONC .  In his records, Jens writes that "XVI Septem Anno Domini 1599 Anna Benckestock was delivered at Phana (Fana) with a Vng Son by Vlrich Meyer."  Since Anna Jonsdatter Benkestok was the stepdaughter of Jens Christenssøn, it is reasonable to believ
1 CONC e that she is the one mentioned here.  Kåre's conclusion: This makes it unlikely that Anne Jonsdatter at Tjøtta is identical to Anna Jonsdatter Benkestok.
