1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT 2024 comment to Ancestry site I saw at library for Thond Tordsen Benkestok 1490-1558.  19 children were born in many places in Norway.  His wife had children after death.  In other words, a mess.  This man with a different surname is Margrethe's gr
1 CONC andfather.
1 CONT 
1 CONT English Translation of above Norwegian 
1 CONT 
1 CONT The Benkestokk seminar: Margrete was married to a Danish man.  Christen Aalborg and resident on Øisund.  It was not new with Danish immigrants, either as priests or traders, but Danes took on more and more ombudsmen and more and more Danes took u
1 CONC p trade in the Nordic countries.  It is not known whether Christen and Margrethe traded, but daughter Beret and her husband Jon Olsen ran hunting farms from Gåsvær and agriculture on Øisund.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Wilhelmine Brandt.  The Benkestok clan, page 6: Margrethe Benkestok.  * with a Danish man, Christen Aalborg, living on Øsund (now Øren) in Melø Fjerding.  From her descends ❝a great hope out of Quinstele❝ (: many descendants on the femal
1 CONC e side.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Wilhelmine Brandt.  Slægten Benkestok, page 123: Margrethe Benkestok, born probably in the late 1580s, probably the youngest child of Jon Benkestok and Birgitte Nielsdatter.  * with Christen Aalborg, who lived on Øsund, ❝a Danish Man❞
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Sources
