1 CONT  Margrete Benkestok's Descendants.  "In the "Series pastorum" for Skjærstad Kald (Presterækken) written down in 1770 by the then parish priest of Skjærstad, Dr. Chr. Fredr. Hagerup, died 30.6.1797 as parish priest in Trondheim, the following i
1 CONC s found, which perhaps should not be omitted here (reproduced in  excerpt) Mr. Jon was a priest in Skjærstad from 1630 - 1650; his grandson "Jon Christensen lived for a time in Øvre Skjærstad and was married to the acquaintance Berit Holgersdatt
1 CONC er, who, along with her sister Lisbeth, had for mother Margrethe, whose grandmother's maternal grandfather must have been  Jon Benkestok" Berit Holgersdatter then gives a very unfavorable testimony for "Evil" - especially directly opposite the loca
1 CONC l parish priest, and then it is added there - that she "moved to Saure in Gildeskål, where she insulted the parish priest there with much evil, Mr. Peder Bruun, and left  just down to Copenhagen to accuse him, even though she had been convicted a
1 CONC t the Provsteret at Gildeslaal 25.8.1727 (personal history journal 1892 by Axel Hagemann) If Jon Benkestok's relationship is correctly stated, perhaps Berit Holgersdatter's mother Margrete's grandmother could be assumed to be a sister  by Berethe C
1 CONC hristensdt.  (Aalborg, and thus a daughter's daughter's daughter of Margrete Benkestok. another possibility is that she is descended from Jon Benkestok's 2nd daughter, Margrethe's only sister, Anna Benkestok, about whom no one knows anything. The n
1 CONC ames Margrethe and Berit, however, almost point to a descent  from Margrethe Benkestok. Source: "Slægen Benkestok" by Wilhelmine Brandt page 123. Somewhat translated by Kari-Elin Røttereng Lillemo
