0 @NFS3442@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Birgitte Nielsdatter (Wilhelmine Brandt) - Berit Nilsdotter (Benkestokk-seminaret).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Wilhelmine Brandt, Slækten Bækestok: Side 5: ( Jon Trondsøn Benkestok til Melø....gift med " en ufri (uadelig) Kvinde Birgitte Nielsdatter, der 1599 levede i Ægteskab med Hr. Jens Christensen, "Læsemester i Bergen. 9 Børn - 1) Torolf, 2) And
1 CONC ers, 3) Trond, 4) Johan, 5)Tord, 6) Christopher, 7) Niels, 8) Anna og 9) Margrethe -:1 og 2.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 1: Om Birgitte Nielsdatters 2den Mand, Hr. Jens Christensen, Læsemester i Bergen, findes udførlige Oplysninger i Biskop Dr. A. Chr Bangs store verk: Den norske kirkes Geistlighed i Reformationsaarhundret. Bl.a sees, at Jens Christensen ca. 1575 b
1 CONC lev "Læsemester" ved Bergen Skole, indtil han ca. 1602 "paa Grund af Alderdom og Skrøbelighed" tok Afsked.2: Dr. Bang har vist dette genealogiske Arbeide sin Interesse ved i ovennævnte Skrift at paapeke en formentlig Feil i det Slægtsregister o
1 CONC ver Fam. Benkestok, som blev paabegyndt i "Nordlands Trompet", 1ste Aarg. S. 138. Den høit ærede Forfatter siger, at ifølge et utrykt Diplom i Rigsarkivet (indeholdende en Arvesag fra 1597) havde Jens Christensen "3 stedbørn" - ikke som alminde
1 CONC lig antaget 9. Vor Kilde er imidlertid ovennævnte Skiftebrev efter Jon Benkestok, (se Bilag II.) samt Ole Jonsens Brev, dat. Meløen 18/1 1747 (Bilag V. b) hvoraf tydelig fremgaar, at Jon Benkestok og Birgitte Nielsdatter havde 9 Børn, 7 Sønne
1 CONC r og 2 Døtre, som alle levede ved faderens Skifte i 1599. - Se også Danmarks Adels Aarbog 1887, samt Arkivar Thomles førnevnte Afhandling i Personalhist. Tidsskrift 2den R. IV. B.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Benkestokk-seminaret. Meløy 14-15 august 1999, utgitt av Adelsprosjektet, revidert av Tore Hermundsson Vigerust: Adelsprosjektets skrifter 3: Side 38: De Benkestokkers Meløy-linje 1570-1695. (Innskrevet av Viggo Vatne, tir. 4. sep. 2012)
1 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT 
1 CONT Om Birgitte Nielsdatter står det "en ufri (uadelig) kvinde" som i 1599 levde i Ægteskab med Hr. Jens Christensen, "Læsemester" i Bergen. Han var lektor ved Latinskolen i Bergen. Han tok avskjed i 1602, på grunn av alderdom og skrøpelighet.
1 CONT 
1 CONT http://vestraat.net/iea-o/p217.htm#i9216
1 CONT 
1 CONT http://www.nermo.org/slekt/d0007/g0000012.html#I8600
1 CONT 
1 CONT Birgitte er også kjent som Berit
1 CONT 
1 CONT Berit Nilsdotter aka Birgitte ?
1 CONT 
1 CONT * BIRTH: ABT 1540, (av uadelig slekt)
1 CONT 
1 CONT * BAPTISM: (Berit)
1 CONT * DEATH: 1620, Nordfjordeid (?) (1599 ?)
1 CONT Family 1 : Jon (2) Trondson BENKESTOK
1 CONT 
1 CONT * MARRIAGE: ABT 1560, (et. at fl. av b. var f., før 31/7-91)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Family 2 : Jens Christenssøn DULL
1 CONT 
1 CONT * MARRIAGE: 1599
1 CONT 
1 CONT Data henta fra http://vestraat.net/rossfjord-o/p111.htm#i11516
1 CONT 
1 CONT Birgitte Nielsdatter (Steinbock)Benkestok was born in 1546 in Meløy, Nordland, Norway. She had one daughter with Jon Trondson Benkestokk of Meloy in 1580. She died in 1620 in Nordfjordeid, Sogn og Fjordane, Norway, at the age of 74.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jon Hallvardson Smør (fl. 1375) was a Norwegian nobleman. He was a son of the knight Hallvard Jonson Smør. In 1375, Jon was the ombudsman of king Haakon VI of Norway. He had two known children, the son Svale, and daughter Ulvhild (whose granddaug
1 CONC hter Birgitte married Trond Tordson Benkestok)
1 CONT 
1 CONT GEDCOM Source
1 CONT 
1 CONT @R450842596@ Ancestry Family Trees Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com. Original data: Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members.
1 CONT 
1 CONT GEDCOM Source
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ancestry Family Tree http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=115559719&pi...
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT The above was copied from the Geni Website.  Note the birth above in English is 1546 but the vitals on Bergitte's PID is 1540.  The 1540 date is also provided above in Norwegian.
1 CONT 
1 CONT (The following was the response given to me in 2024 when I asked about the distance between birth and death locations.
1 CONT they travelled by boat along the coast of Norway, often all the way from Troms and down to Bergen. They brought with them things they could sell in Bergen, and bought things they needed themselves or could sell to the locals up north.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Birgitte moved with her 2nd husband from Meløy in Nordland to Bergen and Norfjordeid on the westcoast.)
1 CONT 
1 CONT The following is the English translation from the Norwegian above.
1 CONT Wilhelmine Brandt, Slækten Bækestok: Page 5: ( Jon Trondsøn Benkestok to Melø....married to " an unfree (indeligible) woman Birgitte Nielsdatter, who in 1599 lived in Ægteskab with Mr. Jens Christensen, "Reader in Bergen. 9 children -  1) Tor
1 CONC olf, 2) Anders, 3) Trond, 4) Johan, 5) Tord, 6) Christopher, 7) Niels, 8) Anna and 9) Margrethe -:1 and 2.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT  1: About Birgitte Nielsdatter's 2nd Husband, Mr. Jens Christensen, Reading Master in Bergen, detailed information can be found in Bishop Dr. A. Chr Bang's great work: The Norwegian Church's Geistlighed in the Reformation Century.  Among other th
1 CONC ings, it can be seen that Jens Christensen approx.  1575 became "Reading teacher" at Bergen School, until he approx.  1602 "paa Grund af Olddom og Skrøbelighed" took leave. 2: Dr. Bang has shown his interest in this genealogical work by pointin
1 CONC g out in the above-mentioned writing a probable error in the genealogical register of Fam.  Benkestok, who was initiated in "Nordlands Trompet", 1st year.  P. 138. The highly respected Author says that according to an unpublished Diploma in the N
1 CONC ational Archives (containing an Inheritance Act from 1597) Jens Christensen had "3 stepchildren" - not as commonly assumed 9. Our source, however, is the above-mentioned Deed of Transfer by Jon Benkestok, (see  Appendix II.) as well as Ole Jonsen'
1 CONC s letter, dated Meløen 18/1 1747 (Appendix V. b) from which it is clear that Jon Benkestok and Birgitte Nielsdatter had 9 children, 7 sons and 2 daughters, all of whom were alive at the time of the father's probate in 1599  - See also Danmarks Ad
1 CONC els Aarbog 1887, as well as Archivist Thomle's aforementioned Afhandling in Personalhist.  Journal 2den R. IV.  B.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT  The bench-seminar.  Meløy 14-15 August 1999, published by Adelsprosjektet, revised by Tore Hermundsson Vigerust: Adelsprosjektets skrifter 3: Page 38: De Benkestokker's Meløy line 1570-1695.  (Entered by Viggo Vatne, Tue. 4 Sep. 2012)
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT  --------------------------------------------------  
1 CONT 
1 CONT  About Birgitte Nielsdatter it says "an unfree (indeligible) woman" who in 1599 lived in Ægteskab with Mr. Jens Christensen, "Læsmeister" in Bergen.  He was a lecturer at the Latin School in Bergen.  He resigned in 1602, due to old age and inf
1 CONC irmity.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  http://vestraat.net/iea-o/p217.htm#i9216
1 CONT 
1 CONT http://www.nermo.org/slekt/d0007/g0000012.html#I8600
1 CONT 
1 CONT Birgitte is also known as Berit
1 CONT 
1 CONT Berit Nilsdotter aka Birgitte?
1 CONT 
1 CONT  BIRTH: ABT 1540, (of indecent lineage)
1 CONT 
1 CONT * BAPTISM: (Berit)
1 CONT 
1 CONT  * DEATH: 1620, Nordfjordeid (?) (1599 ?)
1 CONT 
