0 @NFS3486@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT "Ingeborg. Dog något av åren 1370—1377. Gift först troligen hösten 1345 med riddaren Sten Turesson (Bielke), sedermera riksråd och marsk, död 1350, och sedan på 1350-talet med riddaren Bengt Nilsson (Oxenstierna), vilken i urkunderna nämn
1 CONC es som levande 1357—1371 och blev riksråd 1370."
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Ingeborg. Died sometime between 1370 and 1377. Married first, probably in the fall of 1345, to the knight Sten Turesson (Bielke), later councilor and marshal, died 1350, and then in the 1350s to the knight Bengt Nilsson (Oxenstierna), who is menti
1 CONC oned in the records who was alive 1357-1371 and became councilor in 1370."
1 CONT 
1 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_av_Tofta#TAB_3
0 @NFS3487@ NOTE https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Natt_och_Dag_nr_13#TAB_8
1 CONT Night and day to Ringhult is not a last name, but a place. Ringhult may have been used as an identifier. Ringhalt is a type of ring fastener to hold doors as a henge. Bosson is patronymiv name (or Bo's son or Bosson).
0 @NFS3488@ NOTE Natt och Dag means "night and day" "till" means to or towards, and  Kalmar is an area in Sweden where a population center called Ringhult is located. The phrase carries the meaning "onward night and day to reach Ringhult. A hult is a shallo
1 CONC w place.
