0 @NFS3549@ NOTE TAB 8
1 CONT Bo Bosson , † between 1389 and 1391. (son of Bo Niklisson, tab 7), to Ringshult in Torpa parish. Gunman 1339 and knight already 1356-10-28. Mentioned as councilor as early as 1376. Sealed the councilor's letter in 1382 to the pope with a reques
1 CONC t that the deceased Birgitta Birgersdotter be declared a saint. Last mentioned in the Council in 1389.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children :
1 CONT 
1 CONT Märta Bosdotter , died 1414 at Easter time and buried with her 2nd husband in Vadstena monastery church. Married to Peder Ribbing. Married 1381-08-30 to the knight and councilor Algot Magnusson Sture .
1 CONT Sten Bosson , † 1411. See tab 11.
1 CONT Benkta Bosdotter . Apparently married already before 1368 and probably before 1386 to Turkil Haraldsson . Szabad EÄ corrections
1 CONT Knut Bosson or Canutus Boetiiborn 1359/60. Enrolled in 1381 in the Faculty of Law at the University of Prague and was already cantor in Linköping (Y. Brilioth, Church of Sweden, Kingdom and Pope 1363–1414 (1925), p. 193 ff.). Was one of the twel
1 CONC ve gentlemen who paid tribute to Queen Margaret at Dalaborg in March 1388 (Y. Brilioth, Church of Sweden, Kingdom and Pope 1363–1414 (1925), p. 193 ff.). Was the dean at Linköping Cathedral 1390-06-27. Was bishop (electus) in Linköping 1391-10-
1 CONC 16. Received the Pope's confirmation. 1392 before 1392-05-07, was probably appointed (Y. Brilioth, Church of Sweden, kingdom and papacy 1363–1414 (1925), p. 193 ff.) 1393-01-10 and was solemnly consecrated by Archbishop Henricus Caroli 1393-06 -0
1 CONC 1 in Vadstena, at the same time as St. Birgitta's shrine. Participated in the meeting in Nyköping in 1396. Attended King Erik of Pomerania's coronation in Kalmar and sealed the Kalmar Union. Attended the Lord's Day in Vadstena in 1434 and was forc
1 CONC ed there, by Engelbrekt caught in the collar under threat of being expelled from the peasants, along with the rest of the council to denounce Erik's faith and obedience. Received 1434 on loan from Stegeborg Castle. The council's representative at t
1 CONC he meeting in Halmstad in 1435, where it was decided that King Erik would be recognized again, and shortly before his death visited the Riksdag in Arboga in 1436 and participated in the conditional dismissal of King Erik (NF.). Died 1436-03-12. H
1 CONC e was very eager for the completion of the cathedral in Linköping and for the church building in Vadstena. In his performance of duties, he was rather arbitrary and self-willed. He was accused of having reduced the cathedral's income and transferr
1 CONC ed the property of the bishop's property, by pledging some farms, which had not been redeemed, in order to obtain funds for extensions to his brothers Bo and Benkt.
1 CONT Nils Bosson . Knights and councilors. See Tab. 9.
