0 @NFS3575@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Halvard Toraldsen was born around 1260 in Gulsvik, a long-settled farm community in Flå parish, Buskerud, during a period when Norway was still shaped by medieval rural life and the waning years of the Sverre dynasty. He grew up in a household hea
1 CONC ded by Toralde Gunnarsson and Thorun Haakonsdotter, a family cluster that appears in later genealogical tradition with several siblings, including Ivar, Orm, Thoralda, and the cleric Bishop Salomon Toraldesson of Oslo. Although these relationship
1 CONC s are preserved in modern reconstructions rather than surviving medieval documents, they reflect the family’s remembered position within the local hierarchy of landholding farm families.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Halvard spent his life in Gulsvik, where patronymics—not fixed surnames—were the standard form of identification. His name simply meant Halvard, son of Toralde. He married Margaretha Selvik, and together they raised several sons—Sigurd, Toral
1 CONC de, Gunnar, Sigurd, and Rolf—whose birth years fall between 1290 and 1309. These children continued the Toraldsson line into the 14th century, anchoring the family within the same Buskerud farming landscape.
1 CONT 
1 CONT No contemporary records survive for Halvard, and his profile today is reconstructed from later genealogical tradition rather than archival sources. Even so, the outline of his life is clear: a medieval Norwegian farmer who lived and died in Gulsvik
1 CONC , raising a large family and contributing to the continuity of a lineage remembered in local history. He passed away around 1330, still in the community where he had been born seventy years earlier.
