0 @NFS3749@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Mattis Torgeirson Tufte emerged in the early 1400s as one of the most capable and respected men of Gjerpen Parish in Telemark. Born around 1390 at Tufte Farm, he lived during a period marked by local unrest, shifting alliances, and the Crown’s ef
1 CONC forts to stabilize rural districts. By 1417, he was already serving as a magistrate (lagrettemann) in Skiens county, trusted to witness and validate legal matters.
1 CONT 
1 CONT His reputation grew through the 1430s, culminating in a pivotal role during the aftermath of Hallvard Graatop’s rebellion. In 1439, the farmers of Gjerpen sent Mattis as their envoy to negotiate with Sigrid Niklisdatter Galle of Brunla—widow o
1 CONC f Markvard Buk—after the plundering of Brunla. His mission required diplomacy with both Sigrid and the Council of State, showing he was a man of influence, steady judgment, and political skill. A preserved seal from 1440, bearing his personal hom
1 CONC e mark, confirms his standing among the region’s leading men.
