0 @NFS3774@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Arnbjørn was the son of Ogmund Byre and his wife Ragnhild. He was the only one living of three brothers at the time of his father's probate in 1332.[1]
1 CONT Ambjørn Ogmundsson bid for Byre in 1309 when he was a co-signatory on a letter that told about an agreement Mrs. Ingebjørg på Fet had made with Bishop Kjetil in Stavanger regarding the repair of FinnØy church (see vol. 1, p. 122). We also fin
1 CONC d him mentioned in other contexts up to 1332 when he was responsible for the shift after his parents. Two years earlier, he made a deal with his cousin, Peter Petersson (in the text it says "brørung", i.e. son of the uncle, who must be the son o
1 CONC f No. I above): Peter renounced his noble estate in Byre and Sandanger in Hjelmeland and received three marks of burnt or pure silver from Arnbjørn. Some time after the inheritance settlement in 1332, Arnbjørn moved to Aga, in which he eight part
1 CONC ies. Arnbjørn was married to Magnhild Kjetilsdtr, who, among other things, eight parcels of land in Hodne in Bore parish on Jæren. She is called "Mrs. Magnhild" and had previously been married to the knight Nikolas Munandsson. We know of three ch
1 CONC ildren:
1 CONT 
1 CONT a. Ogmund. He inherited land in Byre, the rine lived in Aga, where he was married to Sigrid Arnesdtr. He is mentioned in several diplomas in the period 1346 60. In his descendants there were prominent men who lived both on Aga and other farms, an
1 CONC d through marriage a connection was made with the Gaute family on Tolga.
1 CONT b. Bjorn. No. 4 below.
1 CONT c. Margrete. She was married to Bård Peterson from Sponheim in Hardanger, shepherd, sysleman and team man. She drew up her will sometime before 25.11. 1322, and then secured "perpetual" tenure at the cathedral in Stavanger. To achieve this, she ga
1 CONC ve her property in Bore, and a piece of land was also laid out as Bård eight south and west of Breiavatnet in Stavanger.
1 CONT (Canon).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Reference Book: Kvinesdal. I.391
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ridder (knight) Arnbjørn Ogmundsen Byre.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ridder Arnbjørn Ogmundsen Byre is mentioned Kvinesdal. I. 391. He was born circa 1285 at Byre, Skartveit, Fister, Norway. He married Magnhild Kjetilsdtr Hodne circa 1310. He was living in 1331.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Magnhild Kjetilsdtr Hodne was born at Hodne, Bore, jæren, Rogaland, Norway. She married Ridder Arnbjørn Ogmundsen Byre, son of Ridder Ogmund Petersen Byre, circa 1310.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sigrid Arnesdtr Aga was born at Aga, Ullensvang, Hardanger, Norway. She died at Aga, Byre, Ullensvang, Hardanger, Norway. She married Amund Arnbjørnsen Skartveit, son of Ridder Arnbjørn Ogmundsen Byre and Magnhild Kjetilsdtr Hodne.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Amund Arnbjørnsen Skartveit was also known as Ogmund Arnbjørnsen Skartveit. He was born circa 1310. He lived in 1346 at Skartveit, Fister, Norway. He married Sigrid Arnesdtr Aga, daughter of Arne Olvirsen Aga and Bergljot Sigurdsdtr Aga. He die
1 CONC d after 1373 at Aga, Byre, Ullensvang, Hardanger, Norway. He is mentioned Kvinesdal. I.391.
