0 @NFS4023@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT 
1 CONT Knight Rane became King Erik Klipping's chamberlain and closest guard commander, but on the night of 22 November 1286, King Erik was murdered during a hunting trip near Viborg. He was found in the morning with 56 wounds and stab wounds, and the bod
1 CONC y was taken to Viborg and placed in the crypt under the cathedral. It was never made clear who had murdered him, but the commoners accused Knight Rane of having allowed the murderers access to the king's bedchamber. In a folk song, he is called th
1 CONC e traitor "who guarded his master like a rogue". At Pentecost 1287, a court was established to decide who should be held responsible for the murder. The nine people known to be guilty, and knight Rane and marshal Stig were considered leaders in th
1 CONC e (political) murder. All nine were sentenced to be outlaws and therefore escaped from the country. The Norwegian king Erik Magnusson took them under his protection, and from 1289 they took part in the war against Denmark. During one of his trips t
1 CONC o Denmark, Rane was captured and taken to Roskilde, where in 1294 he was executed and put on a stake and wheels.
1 CONT When he lived in Norway his residence was at Sæum in Sandsvær
