0 @NFS4094@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Traditionally, Richeza and Przemysł II's marriage is described as happy. Their only child was born on 1 September 1288 in the city of Poznań: a daughter, named Richeza, who later became in Queen consort of Bohemia and Poland as a wife of Wencesla
1 CONC us II and after his death, of Rudolph III of Habsburg.[5]
1 CONT 
1 CONT The news of the birth of her daughter was also the last information about Richeza. She certainly died between 1 September 1288 and before 13 April 1293,[6] most likely between 1289-1292.[7] The reports of Jan Długosz, who placed her next to her hu
1 CONC sband in his royal coronation on 26 June 1295, proved to be erroneous.[6]
1 CONT 
1 CONT The deep and strong feelings of Przemysł II for Richeza are evidenced in two facts: firstly, he named their daughter after her, and secondly, he mentioned her in a document issued on 19 April 1293 where Przemysł II ceded to the Bishopric of Pozna
1 CONC ń the village of Kobylniki as payment for a lamp lit eternally at Richeza's tomb, and also expressed his desire to be buried next to her.[8]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Richeza was buried in the Archcathedral Basilica of St. Peter and St. Paul in Poznań. After Przemysł II's murder in 1296 and following his wishes, he was buried next to her.
