0 @NFS4230@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Johan Månsson ( Night and Day ), born about 1470, died 1520. Lord of Göksholm and Brokind, was a Swedish knight and councillor . Son of Måns Bengtsson (Night and Day) and Ermegard Fickesdotter Bülow.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Murdered Jeppe Bagge and was sentenced for this in 1494 to pay 200 Hungarian gold in settlement to his brothers, the canon in Västerås Jens Bagge , Tuve Nils and Görgen Bagge.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Johan Månsson, who was a supporter of the Sturars, was appointed a councilor in 1501 and in 1510 became governor of Kalmar castle , which he defended against the Danes. Married the second time to Anna Eriksdotter (Bielke) in 1514. Father of Mån
1 CONC s Johansson .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sources 
1 CONT Small Sketch of Owl.pngThis article is based in whole or in part on material from the Nordic family book , "Night and Day 8." , 1904-1926.
1 CONT Further reading 
1 CONT Lars-Olof Skoglund :  Johan Månsson (Night and Day) in Swedish Biographical Lexicon (1987-1989)
