0 @NFS4339@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Magnus Bengtsson ( Night and Day ) , also referred to as Måns , died between 1473 and 1477, was a Swedish knight , councilor and lawman in Närke , lord of Göksholm and Brokind in Östergötland . He was the son of Bengt Stensson (Night and Day
1 CONC ) , but is known to posterity because he killed Engelbrekt Engelbrektsson in the spring of 1436 .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Mentioned as Engelbrekt's squire and armourer in 1434. Magnus Bengtsson participated in the meeting in Arboga in January 1435 when allegiance to King Erik was terminated, and also signed the settlement treaty with him in Halmstad in October 1435
1 CONC . [ 1 ] The motive was probably the conflict that existed between Engelbrekt and Magnus Bengtsson's father and uncles. [ 1 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT He was never punished for the murder, but spent the following years occasionally abroad. In November 1437, he issues a letter in Lund. In March 1439 he went to Gotland with his uncles Bo and Nils Stensson to meet Erik of Pomerania. From there the
1 CONC y returned to Östergötland, where Karlskrönikan claims that he must have fled headlong when he heard how Karl Knutsson chased Nils Stensson and his fleeing men. [ 1 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Mentioned as a knight in 1442.
1 CONT 
1 CONT After that, he is missing from the documents until 1443, when in Örebro, together with his father, he signs a deed of gift. At the 1448 king election, he together with his father, uncle Bo Stensson and the circle around the Oxenstierna family seem
1 CONC s to have taken a stand against Karl Knutsson's election as king. In 1450 he was a member of the Riksråd, and at least in 1450 and 1451 he was a courtier at Brandaborg . At the deposition of Karl Knutsson in 1457, he participated with his relative
1 CONC s in the rebellion, but later in the 1460s seems to have supported the resistance against Jöns Bengtsson (Oxenstierna) , at the siege of Örebro in 1467, Ivar Axelsson handed over responsibility for the siege to Magnus Bengtsson and Arvid Birgerss
1 CONC on Trolle , while he himself went to Stockholm.[ 1 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Magnus Bengtsson also succeeded his father as lawman in Närke. He did not bear the coat of arms of the Night and Day family, but the coat of arms of his mother, Magnus Marinason's family . In 1465 he instituted an anniversary for himself and his f
1 CONC amily at Julita Monastery . In older sources it is stated that he was also buried there, but a source from 1496 shows that he was in fact buried in the Arboga Franciscan monastery. [ 1 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Marriage 
1 CONT Married to Märta Clausdotter (Plata), children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Birgitta Månsdotter
1 CONT Married from 13 November 1458 to Märta Månsdotter ( Tre Rosor till Horshaga ), who lived in 1463, but died in 1466.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Married from 28 September 1466 to Ermegard Fikkesdotter Bülow , children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Kerstin Månsdotter (Night and Day), married to Sigge Larsson (Sparre)
1 CONT Johan Månsson .
1 CONT Sources 
1 CONT ^ [ a b c d e ] Dahlbäck, Göran:  Magnus Bengtsson (Night and Day) in Swedish Biographical Lexicon (1987-1989)
1 CONT External links 
1 CONT Night and Day, 7. Måns Bengtsson in Nordic Family Book (first edition, 1887)
1 CONT http://runeberg.org/anrep/3/0013.html
1 CONT http://www.wisthbf.se/slott-torp/allmaent/Rosman-BS-del1-281.pdf
1 CONT Hans Gillingstam :  Night and Day, family in Swedish biographical lexicon
