0 @NFS4370@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT In a court ruling from 1558, it is said that "Torben Olsen ÿ Quame" (Torbjørn Olavson Sandven?) was sued for estates that had once been sold to "Ivar Arneson in Wale"1) This is probably Herborg in Valen's husband and father of Gaute and Laurits I
1 CONC varssønner and Anna Ivarsdatter. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Herborg Torbjørnsdatter is mentioned as a widow in 1504 and then living in Valen. Her son Gaute Ivarson later lived on this farm, and Laurits Ivarson stayed in Sandvik. Anna Ivarsdatter was possibly married to Jon på Stillufseike in Vats. We hav
1 CONC e told about Haukåsgodset under Ile-Stillufseike, which Laurits Ivarson lost in a lord's court ruling in 1524 to Jon på Stillufseike. This family in Valen and Sandvik belonged to old Norwegian nobility, and a branch of the family was later calle
1 CONC d Slee or Slede, and the family has the right of inheritance to the farm Oma, which the knight Ivar Slede owned.
1 CONT 
1 CONT There can hardly be any doubt that there must be a direct lineage from the knight Ivar Slede and to Ivar or his wife Herborg at Valen in 1504. The name Slede and the noble estate in Oma must confirm this. Gaute Ivarson's father is quite certainly "
1 CONC Ivar Arneson in Wale". He owns land in Sogn and possibly originates from there. The descendants - a branch of it - are called Dall. After Gaute Ivarson comes Olav Bagge as owner of Valen. At least shortly after Gaute's death.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Under the Hovland line we will see that we have Jon Dall at Hovland. His father comes from Sogn and is called lvar Arneson. There must obviously be a family connection between these men with the same name, whose family is called Dall. During the gr
1 CONC eat process about the odel in Hovland, Olav Bagge in Valen is also present. There must be a special reason for that. He must also perhaps have a family connection to these "Dalls".
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT •Gaute Ivarsson in Valen is mentioned in 1512 and onwards, but must have died around 1550. We do not know who he was married to, but we know of 7 children, namely 1) Jon Gauteson to Sveen, 2) Gudrun, married to Nils Clausson, magistrate in Stavan
1 CONC ger, whose son Christoffer Nilsson was also magistrate. (He is mentioned in the process about Opsal in Vikedal), 3) Inger, married to Sverke Jonsson (Theiste?), 4) a daughter was married to Nils Jensson of Semeleng in Valdres. He belonged to the Lo
1 CONC snaætten and was magistrate in Stavanger, 5) Ivar Gauteson, married to Anna Jakobsdatter. They both died before 1578. They had two daughters, Sunniva Ivarsdatter, who was married to Torkel Oma (see about them later) and Karen Ivarsdatter, marrie
1 CONC d to 1) Mikkel, 2) Steffen Erikson Loss. 6) Laurits Gauteson, married to Gyrid Jakobsdatter and 7) Torbjørn Gauteson at Fimreite in Sogn.
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Slektene Velde og Espeland og inngiftede slekter," History book (https://www.nb.no/items/bfd60befe5728733c5f9130b93ca7ce7 need Norway IP to see), Book by Berge Velde, 1957. p.196-7
