0 @NFS4494@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT TORMOD ELVINDSSON KAMP was born about 1400 to unknown parents.  He married Birgitta Olufsdatter Gylenhor about 1431.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Tormod Elvindsson Kamp died about 1459.
1 CONT 
1 CONT BIRGITTA OLUFSDATTER GYLDENHORN was born about 1380 of Elingaard, Onsoy Ostfold, Norway, to  Oluf Torsteinson Gyldenhorn (1370-1433) and Asa Ulfsdatter Lejonbalk (1370-1433.)  She married Tormod Elvindsson Kamp about 1431.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Birgitta Olufsdatter Gylendhorn died 4 August 1433, Ostby gard Skjeberg, Ostfold, Norway, age 53.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 	Child of Tormod Kamp and Birgitta Gyldenhorn
1 CONT 
1 CONT 	1.	*GUNNBORG TORMODSDATTER (1430-1489)
1 CONT +
0 @NFS4495@ NOTE Øystein Guttormson Bratt
1 CONT Birth date: about 1470
1 CONT Father: Guttorm Endridson Bratt
1 CONT Mother: Cecilie Petersdtr.
1 CONT Spouse: Tora Torsdtr. from Tjerne, Ringsaker
1 CONT "Øystein har ått jordegods både i Lom, Dovre og Fron, og han må ha ått Bjølstad i tida 1515-1545"
1 CONT Translation: Øystein has owned estates in Lom, Dovre and Fron, and he must have owned Bjølstad in the period 1515-1545.
1 CONT Son: Peder Øysteinson Bratt
1 CONT Death date: about 1550
0 @NFS4496@ NOTE Østen Guttormsen Bratt or Eystein Guttormsen Bratt
1 CONT Spouse: Tore Torsdatter
1 CONT Children: Sissel Østensdatter Bratt
0 @NFS4497@ NOTE Øystein Guttormsønn Bratt
1 CONT Birth date: about 1475
1 CONT Father: Guttorm Endridesson Bratt
1 CONT Mother: Cecilia Petersdtr.
1 CONT Spouse: Thora Thordsdtr. from Tjerne in Ringsaker.
1 CONT Children: Erich Øysteinsøn, Peder Øysteinsøn Bratt
1 CONT Øystein og Thora på Bjølstad i Heidal hadde seks barn. På denne tid var det meste av Bratts-eiendommene pantsatt, men den eldste sønnen Erich Øysteinsøn hadde da arvet den nevnte garden Arnegård på Dovre. Den pantsatte han til sin yngste b
1 CONC ror, Peder Øysteinsøn Bratt (d. 1556).
1 CONT Translation: Øystein and Thora at Bjølstad in Heidal had six children. At this time, most of the Bratts properties were mortgaged, but the eldest son Erich Øysteinsøn had then inherited the aforementioned farm Arnegård in Dovre. He mortgaged i
1 CONC t to his youngest brother, Peder Øysteinsøn Bratt (d. 1556).
1 CONT Death date: about 1550
1 CONT Source: Veldre Bygdebok, Bye, page 105; FHL book # 948.23/v4 D2s.
