0 @NFS4547@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Custom Fact • 
1 CONT NEILS came to Norway in 1570. That same year, the 22nd of October, he was named in Bergens Korskirke. In 1603, he was sogneprest to Etne and he lived at garden Kambo. 
1 CONT Last Changed: September 17, 2017 by Marcia Lee
1 CONT 
1 CONT Nils Dybdahl Holthe genealogy. Fanaboka In page 429, Lampe: The priests and bishops of the Bergen diocese are mentioned in the Bergesen Book pages 61, 10.
1 CONT 
1 CONT (Research): In 1570 he finished his theological studies and made his way to Norway. Maybe it was adventurous driving him. He was descended from the Danish noble family Bugge, but was himself the son of a common citizen. In the second half of the 15
1 CONC 70s he found the road to Etne. He was first chaplain at Krag in Fana.
1 CONT Last Changed: August 26, 2013 by Gunnar Kjell Rustad	
1 CONT 
1 CONT Nils Dybdahl Holthe genealogy. Fanaboka In page 429, Lampe: The priests and bishops of the Bergen diocese are mentioned in the Bergesen Book pages 61, 10.
1 CONT 
1 CONT He came to Norway about 1570 as resc. in Fana with parish priest Peder Simonsen Krag. He became parish priest in Etne in 1603 and lived on the farm Kambo. His wife was probably the daughter of Hans Teiste who lived at Bjelland, Kvinnherad, d.1624 a
1 CONC nd Brynhilda Benestok d. 1639. (Translated information from Kjell Rustad.)
