0 @NFS4846@ NOTE === (from "Vossaætter", I, L. Kindem)  The B ===
1 CONT (from "Vossaætter", I, L. Kindem)  The Benkestok lineage is one of the oldest families recorded and a Norwegian noble family that continued past the middle ages.  The coat of arms was a shield divided into two fields. One contained half a blue lil
1 CONC y in silver, the other was divided diagonally from the right lower corner in blue and silver. On the helmet were blue and silver on the horns.  The colors were often changed around.  According to one saga, the family got its name because one of th
1 CONC e family members had saved his king, who was under pursuit, by hiding him in the 'high seat' . . . e.g. 'Benkestock'. (There is a partial list of another version on connection from Jon Hallvardson Smør to Trond (?) Benkestok of Melø on page 20 o
1 CONC f the Anders Rustad book.)
