0 @NFS4880@ NOTE === Name approved by FamilySearch ===
1 CONT Alert removed. After recently conferring with FamilySearch on the phone they told me to write this note: The widow fru Skaaden (Mrs.Skaaden) who married Alf Haldorsen, has no first name. Therefore she cannot be identified and temple ordinances wil
1 CONC l not be cleared. She has one ordinance left. This site is associated with the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints and is partly for the purpose of reserving names for temple work. PLEASE, do not change again or I will have to contact Famil
1 CONC ySearch again for further advice.
0 @NFS4881@ NOTE === Clarification for Nina ===
1 CONT Nina,
1 CONT I am not sure who you are talking to at Family Search, but I just had a long conversation with Family Search, and Mrs. Alf Haldorsen is the correct information for the wife of Alf Haldorsen.
1 CONT What is your relationship to Alf or his wife? The purpose of Family Search is to trace your own family tree and make it as accurate as it can be. Alf and his wife are my 15th great-grandparents. How are you related to them?  Marcia Lee
0 @NFS4882@ NOTE === Unknown name ===
1 CONT Unknown or incomplete name for a wife or mother
1 CONT You know her first name but not her maiden last name: Enter the wife's first name, and leave the last name blank.
1 CONT 
1 CONT You know her maiden last name but not her first name: Leave the first name blank, and enter just her maiden name in the last name field.
1 CONT 
1 CONT You do not know any part of her name: Enter Mrs. in the Title field followed by the name of the husband in the appropriate fields.
1 CONT 
1 CONT It is also acceptable to add the father and children to Family Tree and not create a profile for the mother.
