1 CONT TABLE 7
1 CONT Gregers Bengtsson (son of Bengt Jonsson, tab. 6). Appears for the first time on 6 August 1386. Knighted sometime between 1388 and 1391. Still alive 20.9 1396. Must have died 15.2 1405, because his wife was then remarried; mentioned in any case 8.
1 CONC 3 1413 as dead. Gave his wife as a gift land in Jönåkers, Rönö and Öknebo HD in Södermanland. Married 29.1 1387 at Rävelsta in Altuna sn in Simtuna hd in Uppland to Katarina Erengisladotter, daughter of the Riksdag knight Erengisl Nilsso
1 CONC n ( Hammerstaätten ) and his first wife Margareta Bengtsdotter ( Bielke ). Mrs Katarina was remarried on 15.2 1405 to the knight Gustav Leksson (squared shield), who appears for the first time in 1385 and died in 1411. She was still a widow on 29.
1 CONC 4 1435 but died in 1443. A tombstone for her and her daughter by the second marriage can be found in Vadstena monastery church. Her seat was Tyresö in likan, sn in Sotholms hd in Södermanland. Also owned land in Danderyds skplg and Rasbo hd in Up
1 CONC pland, in Jönåkers, Rönö, Sotholms, Svartlösa and öknebo hd in Södermanland, in Aska hd in Östergötland and in Västbo hd in Småland and a farm in Vadstena.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Daughters:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Märta Gregersdotter. Mentioned as a seal witness 7.9 1425. Died 1430. Laid 5.1 1443 buried in the church of the Gråbrödra monastery in Stockholm. Was in all probability already married on 8.3.1413 to Karl Ormsson ( Gumsehuvud ), later knight an
1 CONC d councilor, who was still alive on 9.12.1443, and through this marriage became the mother of Karl Knutsson's queen Katarina. Karl Ormsson was later remarried, first to Ingeborg Bengtsdotter and then to Cecilia Laurensdotter.
1 CONT Ingeborg Gregersdotter. Still alive as a widow in 1459. Together with her husband, she gave away land in Selebo and in Åkers hd in Södermanland and otherwise owned land in Danderyds skplg in Uppland and in Sköllersta hd in Närke. Was 8.5 1416 a
1 CONC nd certainly already 8.3 1413 married to the later Riksdag and lawman in Södermanland Mats Ödgislason ( Lillie av Greger Mattsson's ätt ), who appears for the first time in 1384 and died in 1442, probably 2.8, in any case before 19.9.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Married probably before 1413-03-08 and certainly before 1416-05-08 to Ingeborg Gregersdotter , lived 1459-08-15, when she was seriously ill and probably died in the summer of å., daughter of the knight Greger Bengtsson (Aspenäsätten. The name "
1 CONC Blå-ätten" is obsolete), and Catharina Erengisledotter (Hammerstaätten. The name "Night and Day in the long run" is obsolete). (SBL:23 p62f; SD no.1236; HTF:1964 p12)
