0 @NFS4957@ NOTE === Nobleman ===
0 @NFS4958@ NOTE === Noble Role ===
1 CONT Bengt Turesson Bielke af Åkerö, born around 1291 in Åker, Södermanland, Sweden, was a prominent riksråd (royal councilor) from the Bielke noble family, documented in charters from 1341–1358 ��. He married Ingeborg Magnusdotter (Leijon o
1 CONC r Ulvåten branch) and fathered Kristina Bengtsdotter Bielke (born circa 1333), who wed Gerhard Snakenborg �.Family LineageSon of Ture Kettilsson Bielke af Åkerö (born circa 1260) and Sigrid Nilsdotter (Natt och Dag), Bengt held estates like Kr
1 CONC åkerum and represented high nobility during Magnus Eriksson's reign. His daughter Kristina bridged Swedish Bielke to Mecklenburg migrants �.Noble ContextDied around 1360, Bengt exemplified 14th-century frälsemän alliances pre-Kalmar Union. Thr
1 CONC ough Kristina, Anne Gerhardsdotter Snakenborg, Iliana Åkesdotter Bååt, and Staffan Ulfsson (Tillbakaseende Ulv), his line connects to Vinstorpaätten, Grip, Djäkn, Lejonbalk, and Kafle-Vinge ancestors like Ingeborg Johansdotter Kafle (1462
1 CONC ) �.
