0 @NFS4974@ NOTE === Han er omtalt flere ganger i 1279-1305,  ===
1 CONT Han er omtalt flere ganger i 1279-1305, var riksråd, ridder, baron og en av stormennene i riket. Jon var Gjaldkeri i Bjørgvin, Noreg hovedstad. Gjaldkeren var kongens høyeste embetsmann i byen, holdt orden der, sørget for rettergangen og krevd
1 CONC e inn kongens inntekter. I 1295 møtte han på kongsgården i Danmark ved fredsforhandlingene mellom Norge og Danmark, stadfestet 1296 med kong Eirik et forlik mellom erkebiskopen av Nidaros og hans "kapitel". Eide mye jordegods i ytre Sunnfjord so
1 CONC m han solgte til Munkeliv i 1300.
0 @NFS4975@ NOTE ===  Han var slektas første kjente mann iføl ===
1 CONT  Han var slektas første kjente mann ifølge PA Munch i "Det n orske Folks Historie", død mellom 1320-1350. Hans kone va r ukjent. Han er ikke den samme som Jon Ragnvaldsson.
0 @NFS4976@ NOTE === Harold I Olafson, son of Olaf II, he suc ===
1 CONT Harold I Olafson, son of Olaf II, he succeeded his father at the age of fourteen.  Harald King of the Isle of Man born about 1200 dead in Norway in 1287.  He travelled back to Norway in 1250.  His brother, Olaf the Black and his wife Christina of R
1 CONC oss had a son Magnus Olafson who was the last born Norwegian King in the Isle of Man. The Isle of Man was, from the first, seen by Norwegian Vikings as an attractive, stategic location from which they could dominate the Irish sea.  Consequently, th
1 CONC ere was heavy Scandanavian settlement of the island.  At one point it was part of a Mans-Hebridean realm. Though in theory the ruler of Man owed allegiance to the Kings in Norway, this was more after than not a very "loose" arrangement and, to al
1 CONC l intents and purposes.  Man was an independent kingdom.  Through its independence was somewhat restricted by, first the English in the late 12th century, then the Scots in the early 13th century, it did not come under English Crown control until 1
1 CONC 290. To this day, the Isle of Man maintains it's independent identity (it is not part of the United Kingdom) and has a marked Viking legacy in its language and political institutions.
