1 CONC on in Uppsala Johan Folkason ( Fånöätten ) and probably a cousin of his mother Ramborg Ingevaldsdotter and therefore and with regard to her patronymic, probably the sister of Elena Anundsdotter, who in 1312 mentions Ingevald Estridason ( Hammers
1 CONC taätten ) as her »consobrinus» , as in 1316 by Magnus and Ulf Gudmarssons ( Ulvåsaätten ) are called »cognatus» as well as the lawman Knut Magnusson ( Tyrgils Knutsson's family ) and his brother the knight Gustav Magnusson, who also had th
1 CONC e right to inherit after Johan Folkason, who in 1318 sealed the first will of Lars Ulfsson and Ingrid Anundsdotter.
