1 CONC . y's will in 1335 and probably had a son named Holmger, named after one of his early deceased uncles.
1 CONT 2. Holmger Ulfsson (died), 1304-1311. See tab. 6.
1 CONT 2. An unnamed daughter. Still alive in 1326. Was married no later than 1325 to the knight Birger Magnusson ( Magnus Marinason's family ), who then calls Lars Ulfsson his "gener" and in 1335 seals Ulf Holmgersson d. y's will but remarried no later t
1 CONC han 1334 to Katarina Olofsdotter and died sometime between 1349 and 1352 of starvation in Russia, apparently as a participant in Magnus Eriksson's Russian war.
1 CONT 2. Catherine. Was married in 1338 to the knight Ulf Magnusson ( Lejonbalk ), who appears in the records from 1320 and died in 1343. Probably previously married to a Torsten and identical to the wife Katarina Ulfsdotter, who in 1346 is called the mo
1 CONC ther of Ingeborg Torstensdotter in her will, where children of Torkel Andersson appear as witnesses.
