0 @NFS5101@ NOTE === Family linage  ===
1 CONT Sigrid Sparre, born around 1241 in Värend, Kronoberg, Sweden, appears in some genealogical records as a noblewoman from the Sparre family (possibly Natt och Dag branch), married to Ture Kettilsson Bielke af Åkerö (born circa 1260). She links ear
1 CONC ly Småland gentry to Bielke estates like Kråkerum during Folkunga consolidations ��.Family LineageMother of Bengt Turesson Bielke af Åkerö (born 1291), Nils, Erik, and others, Sigrid connects Sparre's three lily pads heraldry to Bielke's re
1 CONC d beam. Descendants through Bengt and his daughter Kristina Bengtsdotter Bielke (born circa 1333, married Gerhard Snakenborg) extend to Snakenborg-Bååt-Ulv-Vinstorpa lines.Historical ContextVärend's lagman networks placed Sigrid amid 13th-centur
1 CONC y frälsemän alliances pre-Kalmar Union. Her era overlaps Birger Jarl's reforms; through Kristina, ties reach Grip, Djäkn, Lejonbalk, Kafle-Vinge, and figures like Ingeborg Johansdotter Kafle (1462) �.
