0 @NFS5105@ NOTE === Lendmann (Baron) Gaut Jonsson Ornes/Mel ===
1 CONT Gaut appears in several of the late sagas (e.g., Håkon Håkonssons saga; Sturlunga saga), and, given his political prominence, much is known about his life. He was a Baron (lendmann), as well as Syslemann (governor) of Sunnhordland, and Rådgiva
1 CONC r (advisor) to King Håkon Håkonsen IV. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Recent research (e.g., Magerøy 1988; Stang 2020) provides strong evidence that he was born at Ornes in Stryn (now Luster), and is the son of Jon Gautsen Ornes (with the old Ænes being now understood as a mistranscription of Ornes).
1 CONT 
1 CONT We do not have a name for his spouse, and history only records the names of two children: Finn Gautsen and Gaut Gautsen. Both became barons.
1 CONT 
1 CONT I have worked to revise this part of the tree to reflect what is historically known.
