0 @NFS5110@ NOTE === she has no known parents.  she was known as Sigrid the Fair ===
1 CONT According to Brilioth, 1922, p. 194, a story is told by the abbess of Vadstena (where Bengt is confused with a brother of the King), which states that he married Sigrid "the Fair," of low birth and against the King's wishes. The latter sent him a c
1 CONC ape half made of cloth-of-golf, and half of wadmal to show him how inappropriate a combination the marriage was, but Bengt responded by having the wadmal part stitched with gems and pearls and eventually the King is won over by the charms of Sigrid
1 CONC . This story was further popularised (and further confused) in an 1865 play called "The Wedding at Ulfåsa". Brilioth closes by stating that none of this can be proven and that only the names of Bengt and Sigrid can be evidenced.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Wernstedt, 1957, p. 40
1 CONT Brilioth, Y. (1922) "Bengt Magnusson" in Boëthius, B. (ed.) Svenskt Biografiskt Lexikon, vol. 3. Stockholm: Albert Bonnier, pp. 193-195.
1 CONT Wernstedt, F. (1957) Äldre Svenska frälsesläkter, vol. I.1. Stockholm: Riddarhusdirektionen.
