0 @NFS5124@ NOTE === Who Is Inga Vikingsdatter? ===
1 CONT There is no historical evidence that Gaut Jonsen Mel married an Inga Vikingsdatter; this relationship may be the result of confusion about the Ænes/Ornes, Torsnes, & Mel-Hatteberg family lines. Perhaps this Inga is meant to be the daughter of Viki
1 CONC ng på Torsnes, who married a man name Kalv, giving rise to the Torsnes family? Regardless, there is no basis for this relationship, and it probably should be undone.
0 @NFS5125@ NOTE === Familjeförhållande ===
1 CONT var en svensk högreståndsperson tillhörande Bjälboätten som ska ha levat på 1100-talet. Enligt den danska historikern Saxo var han son till Folke den tjocke och prinsessan Ingegärd Knutsdotter av Danmark. Därmed så härstammade han, via si
1 CONC n mormor Adele av Flandern, tretton led bakåt från Karl den Store samt tio led bakåt från Alfred den Store.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Den svenska s.k. "Genealogia folkungorum", som är trehundra år yngre än Saxo men åberopar sig på en gammal uppteckning i Varnhem, är källan till tillnamnet Snivil och uppgiften att Bengt skall ha varit fader till Birger Brosa, Magnus minnesk
1 CONC öld och Karl Döve samt farfar till Birger jarl.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Källorna nämner ingenting om huruvida Bengt hade jarlvärdighet eller övriga uppgifter.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Tillnamnet snivil kan enligt Lagerqvist och Åberg tolkas antingen som den lille eller som näsvis bängel eller ha syftat på snor.
0 @NFS5126@ NOTE === Sources: ===
1 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Folkesson-18
1 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bengt_snivil
1 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDISH%20NOBILITY.htm#BirgerBrosadied1202
1 CONT 
1 CONT BENGT Folkason "Snivel", son of FOLKE "den digre/the Fat" Jarl in Sweden & his wife Ingegerd of Denmark (-bur [Varnhem Abbey]).  Saxo Grammaticus names Ingegerd's sons Knud and Bengt[9].  Jarl in Sweden. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT m ---.  The name of Bengt´s wife is not known. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bengt & his wife had three children: 
1 CONT 
1 CONT 1.         BIRGER "Brosa" (-9 Jan 1202). 
1 CONT 2.         MAGNUS "Minnesköld" (-killed in battle near Lena 31 Jan 1208).  
1 CONT 3.         KARL .  “Byrgerus dux magnus et Karolus fratres eius” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/85] under which “Kanutus…Rex Sweorum atque Gotthorum” donated property to the monks of Juleta kloster[36].  “Byrgo Sweorum et Guttorum d
1 CONC ux…Philippus frater meus, Magnus et Karolus fratres ducis…” witnessed a charter dated to [1167/99] under which “K…Sweorum rex filius Herjcjs itjdem regis” donated property to Nydala kloster[37]. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT  
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bengt was the son of Folke "the Fat" Ingevaldsson and Ingegerd Knutsdotter of Denmark (daughter of king Canute IV of Denmark).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bengt Folkesson , known as Bengt snivil or Bengt snivel , was a Swedish high-ranking person belonging to the Bjälbo family who is said to have lived in the 12th century . According to the Danish historian Saxo , he was the son of Folke the Fat an
1 CONC d Princess Ingegärd Knutsdotter of Denmark . Thus he descended, via his grandmother Adele of Flanders , thirteen lines back from Charlemagne and ten lines back from Alfred the Great .
1 CONT 
1 CONT The Swedish so-called "Genealogia folkungorum", which is three hundred years younger than Saxo but refers to an old record in Varnhem , is the source of the surname Snivil and the information that Bengt must have been the father of Birger Brosa , M
1 CONC agnus minnesköld and Karl the Deaf as well as the grandfather of Earl Birger .
1 CONT 
1 CONT The sources do not mention anything about whether Bengt had earlship or other information.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The nickname snivil can, according to Lagerqvist and Åberg , be interpreted either as the little one or as a snob or have referred to snot .
1 CONT 
1 CONT See also 
1 CONT Bjälboätten
1 CONT Sources 
1 CONT Bengt in Nordisk familjebok (second edition, 1904)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bengt had at least three children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT The Riksjarl Birger Brosa
1 CONT Magnus Minnesköld
1 CONT Charles the Deaf
1 CONT Notes
1 CONT The existence of the wife connected here to Bengt, Ulfhild Björnsdotter, is highly disputed by modern historians.[1]
1 CONT One of the sources that mention Bengt Snivil as a son of Folke is Saxo Grammaticus, a Danish historian who lived around 1200 AD.[2]
1 CONT Folke the fat married Ingerd, the daughter of the in 1086 murdered king Knut the Holy. With her, he had the sons Bengt and Karl and through them the grandsons Birger Brosa, Karl the deaf, and Magnus Minniskiöld.[3]
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT ↑ Arne Blom, Anforum, Genealogi.se
1 CONT ↑ Harrison, Dick (2002). Jarlens sekel: en berättelse om 1200-talets Sverige. Stockholm: Ordfront. p.182
1 CONT ↑ Nordisk Familjebok / Uggleupplagan 2. Armatoler - Bergsund 1349 - 1350 (1904)
1 CONT Folkungaätten, Svenskt biografiskt lexikon (art av Hans Gillingstam), hämtad 2016-05-28
1 CONT Folkungaätten, Adelsvapen-Wiki
1 CONT Nordisk familjebok (1908) p.792
1 CONT Nordisk familjebok (1904) p.1350
1 CONT "Bengt Snivil," Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia, (accessed May 28, 2016)
