0 @NFS5180@ NOTE === Historical Role ===
1 CONT Ulf Karlsson (Ulv), from the Folkungaätten branch known as Ulv, was born approximately 1230 (records vary to 1238 or 1247–1248) in Stensta, Örebro (Närke), Sweden, and died in 1281, buried at Skänninge Abbey ��. He served as Sweden's firs
1 CONC t drots (marshal) in 1276 under King Magnus Ladulås and was a riksråd (royal councilor) and knight, representing the crown at the Göta älv peace meeting �.Family LineageSon of Karl Karlsson (Ulv) and possibly Helena Petersdotter or a Lejonbal
1 CONC k daughter, he married Katarina (or Ramfrid Gustavsdotter Lejonbalk) and fathered Filip Ulfsson (Ulv) (born circa 1265), directly linking to the Tillbakaseende Ulv chain through Staffan Ulfsson and Kristina Staffansdotter Ulv's marriage to Bengt Ud
1 CONC dsson Vinstorpaätten ��.Historical RoleAs a close kinsman to Magnus Ladulås, Ulf held estates like Akaerö and mills in Torshälla, wielding influence during Folkunga consolidation with the winged arrow (pilspets) coat of arms evolving into t
1 CONC he rear-facing wolf. His prominence ties the early 13th-century nobility to the full Kafle-Vinge ancestry traced from Ingeborg Johansdotter Kafle (1462) �.
0 @NFS5181@ NOTE === Family  linage ===
1 CONT Ulf Karlsson (Ulv), from the Folkungaätten Ulv branch, was born approximately 1230 (variants include 1238 or 1247–1248) in Stensta, Örebro (Närke), Sweden, and died in 1281, buried at Skänninge Abbey ��. As Sweden's first drots (marshal
1 CONC ) in 1276 under King Magnus Ladulås, he was a knight, riksråd, and key representative at the Göta älv peace treaty �.Family LineageSon of Karl Karlsson (Ulv) and possibly Helena Petersdotter or a Lejonbalk daughter, he married Katarina or Ram
1 CONC frid Gustavsdotter Lejonbalk, fathering Filip Ulfsson (Ulv) (born circa 1265) and Ingeborg Ulfsdotter. This directly continues the Tillbakaseende Ulv chain to Staffan Ulfsson, Kristina Staffansdotter Ulv, and her marriage into Vinstorpaätten �
1 CONC �.Noble AchievementsA close kinsman to Magnus Ladulås, Ulf owned Akaerö estate and Torshälla mills, using the winged arrow (pilspets) coat of arms that evolved into the rear-facing wolf. His prominence during Folkunga consolidation links the 1
1 CONC 3th-century high nobility to the full Kafle-Vinge descent from Ingeborg Johansdotter Kafle (1462) �.
