0 @NFS5197@ NOTE === Noble context  ===
1 CONT Bengt Jönsson Bielke af Åkerö, born circa 1220 possibly in Vapnö, Halland, Sweden, was an early member of the Bielke noble family during the 13th century. He fathered Kettil Bielke av Åkerö (born around 1235), continuing the clan's lineage am
1 CONC ong Sweden's frälsemän (knightly freeholders) with red beam heraldry ��.Family LineageBengt married Ingeborg Magnusdotter af Ulvåsa, linking Bielke to Ulvåsaätten alliances amid Folkunga expansions. His descendants include Ture Kettilsso
1 CONC n Bielke af Åkerö (born circa 1260), Bengt Turesson Bielke af Åkerö (born 1291), and Kristina Bengtsdotter Bielke (born circa 1333, married Gerhard Snakenborg).Noble ContextActive in Småland-Västergötland estates like Åkerö during Birger J
1 CONC arl's era, Bengt represented regional gentry pre-Kalmar Union. Through Kristina's line to Snakenborg-Bååt-Ulv-Vinstorpa, Grip, Djäkn, Lejonbalk, and Kafle-Vinge, his ancestry connects to figures like Ingeborg Johansdotter Kafle (1462) �.
