0 @NFS5202@ NOTE === Who Is Gaut på Ornes? ===
1 CONT There is no historical documentation that supports the notion that Gaut/Gaute was a son of Jarl Ogmund Ormsen/Ormsson. Information from the sagas (following the outline from Foundation for Medieval Genealogy) indicate that Ogmund Ormsson had one so
1 CONC n (Munan) and one daughter (Astrid). Note also that Ornes (Solvern, Sogn og Fjordane--now part of Luster kommune in Vestland--not Kvinnherad, Hordaland) is the actual place name for Ænes. Magerøy (1988, ‘Urnes stavkyrkje, Ornes-ætta og Ornes-g
1 CONC odset.’ Historisk Tidsskrift nr. 2) demonstrates that Ænes was a mistranslation of Ornes, a place name in Sverris Saga. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sverris Saga does mention 'Gaut af Órnesi', but we do not know his father's name. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT That Gaut på Ornes came from a prominent family seems pretty clear. It is likely his father was the funder for and builder of one of the most famous surviving Stave churches in Norway, built c1130 (Stang 2020). And the prestige of the Ornesæatte
1 CONC n continued in the lines of his two known sons: Jon and Munan Gautsen. But for this line of the Ornesætten, any claims to further ancestry are, at best, spurious, and should be treated with great skepticism.
0 @NFS5203@ NOTE ===  "Ænes kan muligens være Ornes i Sogn. G ===
1 CONT  "Ænes kan muligens være Ornes i Sogn. Gaut hører formodentl ig til ættekretsen som utgikk fra Horda-Kåre. Til samme ætt ekretsen mener man også at Erling Skjaglson hørte." Det e r nokså sikkert at Ænes  er en skrivefeil og at det er Orn
1 CONC e s i Sogn det gjelder.
