0 @NFS5214@ NOTE ===  Another record gives his name as Audun  ===
1 CONT  Another record gives his name as Audun Vigleiksen in Borg withties to Østensjø, Ås, Akershus also. Audun  is our earliest known ancestor mentioned. However, sincehis name was probably Audun Torersson, then his father Torer wasthe earliest. We d
1 CONC o not know who his father was, but his motherwas the oldest daughter of Olav Haavardsson and a sister to KingHaakon Haakonsson's mother. Audun was well thought of and wellto do and lived in the seacoast city of Sarpsborg as his wife'sgrandmother wa
1 CONC s Queen Ingerid Ragnvaldsdatter (King HaraldGille, and her father was a brother to Queen Ragna of Norway,wife of King Eystein who was a son of Queen Ingerid. He may mayhave gotten them through having close ties to nobility. Early in the 1200s, ther
1 CONC e lived a nationally important man whoowned a house in Borg (Sarpsborg) and was called Audun of Borg.His name was undoubtedly Audun Toresson. Audon of Borg was akinsman (sister-in-law) of Inga from Varteig, mother of KingHåkon Håkonsson. Inga bec
1 CONC ame friendly (and pregnant) with KingHåkon Sverresson when he was visiting with his friend Audun inSarpsborg in 1203. "She was also high born and a "handsomegirl". Håkon Sverresson died suddenly New Year's Day of 1204.The legend is that she (Inga
1 CONC ) described him as one handsomeyoung man. (He was 28-30 years old and was allegedly poisoned byhis stepmother, Margreta, at a Christmas dinner. King Sverre hadfour children, including Håkon, before he married Margreta, thesister of Swedish King Kn
1 CONC ut Eriksson and he had only onedaughter with Margreta. Margreta fled back to Sweden after thepoisoning. Inga fled from the south with her newborn son sincethe Danish Bagler group took over control in 1204. She went toTrondelag (Nidaros, which is no
1 CONC w Trondheim) to the Birchlegs.(She had the baby at Folkisberg parsonage in Eidsberg parish andthe priest was aware that the father was King Håkon Sverresson.The trip north through the mountains took place at Christmas1205 when the baby king wa
1 CONC s 1 1/2 years old.)  Inga was latermarried to a Birchlegs leader, Vegard from Verdal. Inga of Varteig was identified as "Inga Olafsdatter fra Varteig,1183-1235" in one family genealogy on Internet. This was a harrowing trip and is described in mor
1 CONC e detail in theSorenson history book, Norway . She passed through HamarChristams Eve and then on through Lillehamar and over themountain where Håkon was carried by skiers to Nidaros. KingHåkon Sverresson had been friendly with the Birchlegs facti
1 CONC on.Then, the following took place in 1217 when Håkon was associatedwith Earl Skule and had become king. W.D.I. When they arrived in Nidaros, the earl was received with utmostcourtesy by the archbishop, but the latter refused to show theproper hono
1 CONC r to the king.; and the reason being that there wassome doubt as to whether Håkon was really the son of HåkonSverresson, it was agreed that his mother, Inga of Varteig, wasto submit to the ordeal of fire. This was done in Bergen in thepresence o
1 CONC f the king, the earl, the archbishop, and otherbishops and chiefs. The result was in every way satisfactory.The church declared that King Håkon had proved his paternity,and Earl Skule was for the time being apparently reconciled withthe king. Audu
1 CONC n had at least two daughters and two sons. The sons: TorerAnundsson Tinghatt, who was a judge and owned Sørum inSørum Anund Audunsson, a lawyer in Oslo. The two daughters: Sigrid, who married Hugleik of Hegranes in Jølster. Alsorecorded as Gudru
1 CONC n who married Hugleik Smør (Semeur) Jonsen.,then Øystein Ormsen, and last, Arne Smidsen. Ragnild who married Bjørn Kamp. Inga and Vegard had a son, Olav, who was married to Ragndid,daughter of Earl Skule of the noble Reins family in Trondelag.(S
1 CONC kule's half brother Inge was interim King between HåkonSverresson and Håkon Håkonsson and he kept trying to become thepermanent king and did proclaim himself king in 1239 and waskilled by the Birchlegs in 1240.) They had sons Håkon and Olav.Rag
1 CONC ndid was a sister of King Håkon Håkon sson's queen. (Themarriage was arranged to try to bring peace between Skule andHåkon Håkonsson.) Vegard was undoubtedly from Stein farm inVerdal, and his son Olav was called Olav of Stein, but also OlavRagn
1 CONC didarson. At that time, surnames after a mother signified that the motherwas of a very high ranking family. Her name was also writtenRagnrid and Ragneid. Skule's mother was Ragndid from Kvein inValdres. Also, the daughter of Audun of Borg was of pa
1 CONC rticularhigh birth, for Bjørn Kamp was sometimes called AmundRagnildsarsson. In addition, the son of Ragnild's daughterKristin was also called Gudleik Kristensson after his mother.Another indication of Audun's relationship with King Håkon comesfr
1 CONC om a legal brief that law expert Audun Hugleiksson prepared onMarch 24, 1279 which he closed by claiming that his grandfather,Audun of Borg, had obtained Bjarka (Bjørke) farm in Frogna fromKing Håkon.
