0 @NFS5233@ NOTE ===  Name varies in records. One is Sigurd A ===
1 CONT  Name varies in records. One is Sigurd Amundsen. Another isNN(Oleson) Aaleson. Olav was a prefect in Hedmark. He was named in King Håkon Håkonssons Saga in 1240 as a friendof the King. He was the head of the Sudreim farm in Sorum inRomerike. Th
1 CONC e Ribbungs and Birchlegs were battling in 1224 andthe Ribbungs were raiding the Romerike area and then going backto friends in Varmeland. The Ribbungs came upon his farm, butOlav was at a wedding at Leyrin (Løren) farm in Sorum. They tookhis 20 me
1 CONC n prisoner and then killed them. Olav assembled a newgroup and took battle and ran them off but was killed shortlyafter. The king, hearing of the killings deplored the act andsaid that Olav's mother was the daughter of King Harald Gilleand his fath
1 CONC er was Aale of Varg, the king's liegeman inRomerike. Olav was the liegeman of Hedmark as early as 1218.Sudreim farm was named first in 1331, when Haftor Jonson livedthere. King Håkon invaded Varmeland with 2400 men early in 1225, burnedmany grea
1 CONC t houses, but did not succed in meeting the Ribbungs inbattle. Children: Ivar, our ancestor.
