0 @NFS5240@ NOTE === When Mary was growing up in Kerrisdale P ===
1 CONT When Mary was growing up in Kerrisdale Presbyterian Church, there was a Carson family who were devoted church members.  One of their daughters, Sadie, remained single for many years, but finally married a much older man named Giske - we thought thi
1 CONC s name unusual.  He was no prince, but was comfortably off, I believe he was a fisherman (retired).  They bought the house on the corner of 4lst Avenue and Elm Street, worth about $400,000. today (1995).  Sadie (Carson) Giske took over my job in th
1 CONC e Admitting Office at St. Paul's Hospital when I progressed to the Cashier's office.  She continued to work there for years.  Only now do I discover her old husband was Norwegian.
