1 CONC ians agree that most likely the data is reasonable correct. This is certainly not the case for his parents. It is not appropriate to extend this line without credible evidence that meets genealogical research standards. There are very many conscien
1 CONC tious and dedicated family history workers who want to include every possible name to make sure that no one is left out of their temple work. Some feel that in the dark ages that deductions have to be made because of the lack of credible sources fo
1 CONC r this period. There are important reasons why the Church will not generally authorize temple work to be done after the 15th century.
