0 @NFS5407@ NOTE ===  Bishop Andres in Oslo and Baron Audon H ===
1 CONT  Bishop Andres in Oslo and Baron Audon Hugleiksson proclaimed  onMarch 24, 1279 in a document of Bjarka(Bjørke) in Frogn  (DN II19) that Jon Holteson had given to Oslo Cathedral. Audun, whohad newly acquired favor from  the crown, released Bjark
1 CONC a fromthe church and turned it over to the crown. Halvard's Church wassubstituted consequently, a farm Audun Hugleiksson took afterJon Holteson: 2 hefseldebol and 10 øyer silver in Audnar Formuin Romerike, a like amount in Ganstad in Romerike, 1he
1 CONC lfseldebol and 1/2 mark in Torsegg in Romerike, 1 hefeldeboland 6 øyer silver in Vigstein in Nannestad, 6 øyresbol in Oppiin Vesong, 10 øyresbol in Sogarden and 7 øyresbol in NegardenBryn in Aker, 4 øyresbol in Bardarud in Aker, 8 øyresbol in
1 CONC Østre O in Aker, 10 øyresbol in Okern in Aker and 10 øyresbol inStore Bø in Follo. Jon Holteson was a large landowner, so this only could have beenof the goods he owned.  Audun Hugleiksson said at the end of thedocument that his mother's fathe
1 CONC r (Audon Borg) had obtainedBjarka from King Hakon. He lived at Holter in Nes and Bjerke (Drøbak) In Follo.
