0 @NFS5495@ NOTE === Israel Birgerssons family, Only two children are known. ===
1 CONT 
1 CONT Hans hustru nämns (utan namn?) i flera testaments och arvsdokument, varvid vid åtminstone ett tydligt visar Israel Birgerssons sigill. Minst två barn är kända:[1]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sonen Peter Israelsson var väpnare, och stod märkligt nog under striderna om Sveriges krona på kung Magnus och kung Håkans sida. Med Peter Israelssons död utslocknade Finstaätten på manssidan.
1 CONT Dottern Helena Israelsdotter var en av minst fem kända hustrur till kung Karl Knutssons morfar Karl Ulfsson (Sparre av Tofta), och har förmodats vara Karl Knutssons mormor, men deras äktenskap var barnlöst. Karl Knutssons mor Margareta Karlsdot
1 CONC ter föddes i själva verket i något av morfaderns två sista kända giften.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT His wife is mentioned (without a name?) in several wills and inheritance documents, whereby at least one clearly shows Israel Birgersson's seal. At least two children are known:[1]
1 CONT 
1 CONT The son Peter Israelsson was a squire, and strangely enough, during the battles for Sweden's crown, he was on the side of King Magnus and King Håkan. With the death of Peter Israelsson, the Finsta family died out on the male side.
1 CONT The daughter Helena Israelsdotter was one of at least five known wives of King Karl Knutsson's grandfather Karl Ulfsson (Sparre av Tofta), and has been presumed to be Karl Knutsson's grandmother, but their marriage was childless. Karl Knutsson's mo
1 CONC ther Margareta Karlsdotter was in fact born in one of the last two known marriages of the maternal grandfather
