0 @NFS5765@ NOTE === Kan ikke være den Jon Teiste som ble dre ===
1 CONT Kan ikke være den Jon Teiste som ble drept i 1607 fordi Anne Kruckow døde ca. 1602 og var gift 2.gang med Anders Nilsen. 1549-1562 forlenet med Andenes Len. Var død 1562. Se Norsk Magasin I, s.209. Væpner. 1525 erkebiskop Olufs Ombudsmann i Ber
1 CONC gen, og 1531 hans Kjøgemester og levde i 1547. Trolig død før 20 feb 1555, da Andenes Len dette året ble gitt til Nils Trolle.
0 @NFS5766@ NOTE === A google translate of part of the memory ===
1 CONT "Elin, together with her brother Hallvard, must have been entitled to the large farm Tom in Råde, where she inherited a share of the farm together with a number of other properties in Østfold and Sweden on probate after her father Olav. Tom was a
1 CONC lready divided between several owners in the early 14th century, and it is doubtful whether Elin's father lived there. The brother Hallvard also had descendants, although we currently have no further knowledge of them. The many disputes about Tom'
1 CONC s patrimonial right around 1400 seem to have their background in the fact that the parties involved were all descendants of Elin or Hallvard.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Guttorm and Elin married before 23.02.1317. Guttorm then inherited with his wife from his unknown father-in-law various estates in Østfold, Bohuslen and Sweden (DN VIII 49, "Regesta Norvegica" III, no. 1013):
1 CONT "Witness letter about succession written on Thufn (Tom) from Odd in Hisingby, Åmunde in Åker, Arne in Kalszrud, Sæmund in Rød, Bård in Åker and Aslak in Hiaranderud:
1 CONT Was present when Hallvard Olavsson and Elin Olovsdatter, represented by her husband Guttorm Eiriksson, succeeded their father. Hallvard got farm lots in Tom, Hiaranderud, Røstad, Breivik with the salmon hatchery and Møllerød. Guttorm got Lundene
1 CONC , Midbøn with all clearing sites, Hellubek and Mauratorpe. They also changed the following farms in Sweden: Røflile, Hestengene, Miunubækin, Dyrræbergh and Vestby nedre and the mills at Dalli, Klofonæ, Hellunæ and Issekverna.
1 CONT Witnesses: Peter Olavsson, Klemen Gudbrandsson, Peter Sæmundsson, Arnulv Alvsson and many other good men.
1 CONT Sealed by Hallvard Olavsson and the issuers".
1 CONT 
1 CONT The farm Tom in Råde was in the 14th century divided into two, a northern and a southern farm. The 12 øresbol that Hallvard got was the northern farm in Tom.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Guttorm and Elin had the following children (at least):
1 CONT Olav, mentioned in 1338, mentioned as cross brother in Oslo in 1348, probably died in the autumn of 1349.
1 CONT Gjardar, mentioned in 1348, probably died in the autumn of 1349.
1 CONT Gudrun, married 1st time to Bergsvein Baardsen in Asker, mentioned 1344-61,
1 CONT married 2nd time to Herr Jon Toraldesen, mentioned 1351-70.
1 CONT Gyda, married to the squire Alv Paalsen, mentioned 1337-44.
1 CONT Gjertrud, married to the fairy herder and armorer Torgaut Jonsen [Smør], mentioned from 1350, died ca. 1375.
1 CONT A daughter (unknown name), probably married to the armourer(?) Peder Olavsen, mentioned in 1339.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The daughter Gudrun and Bergsvein had children (at least):
1 CONT Elin, mentioned 1380-99, died ca. 1422,
1 CONT married 1st time to the knight Herr Haakon Eivindsen, mentioned in 1372, died approx. 1380,
1 CONT married a second time to the gunsmith Haakon Munansen [Stumpe].
1 CONT Gunhild, mentioned 1390-1422, married to the knight Agmund Berdorsen [Bolt], mentioned 1368-1418.
1 CONT Guttorm, died young, unmarried and childless.
1 CONT The daughter Gyda and Alv Paalsen had a son
1 CONT Hallvard Alvsen, to Sandbu, squire and governor, mentioned from 1379, died in 1429,
1 CONT married 1st time to Jartrud Paalsdatter (she married 1st time to Gunnar Erlandsen),
1 CONT married 2nd time to Gjertrud Paalsdatter.
1 CONT The daughter Gjertrud and Torgaut had the daughter
1 CONT Ulvhild, mentioned 1398-1413, married to the squire and governor Benkt Nikolasson, mentioned 1378-98.
1 CONT The daughter with an unknown name had a son Olav Pedersen, mentioned 1365-82, married to a Simonsdatter.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Mrs Elin was still alive on 07.03.1348 when their two sons are mentioned in a deed of gift from [Mr] Guttorm Eiriksen (DN IV 324, "Regesta Norvegica" V, no. 1028):
1 CONT (next part did not translate, not Norwegian?
