0 @NFS5807@ NOTE === source ===
1 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bo_Nilsson_(Grip)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bo Nilsson (Grip) , born in the 1420s , died in 1465 or 1466 in Söderköping , was a Swedish knight and councillor .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Biography
1 CONT Bo Nilsson was the son of knight and councilor Nils Erengislesson ( Hammerstaätten ) and Katarina Knutsdotter (Grip) (died 1449 / 52 ), daughter of Knut Bosson (Grip) and Ermegard Bylow (ca. 1364-1421).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Family
1 CONT Bo Nilsson married around 1454 Beata Karlsdotter (Vasa), daughter of the Riksdag Karl Kristiernsson (Vasa) and Ebba Eriksdotter ( Krummedige ). Together they had the son Nils Bosson (Grip) (1460-1522).
1 CONT 
1 CONT He is considered the progenitor of the younger family Grip . This by adopting the mother's family coat of arms, a grappling head. This family Grip died out on the sword side with Bo Nilsson's grandson Baron Nils Birgersson Grip in 1592 .
