1 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Lillie_af_Greger_Mattssons_%C3%A4tt_nr_6
1 CONT 
1 CONT TABLE 2
1 CONT Greger Mattsson (son of Matts Ödgislesson, Tab. 1), to Tyresö in the parish of the same name, Stockholm County, which he inherited from his grandmother. Was a squire in 1440, knight 1443-06-15 and councilor in 1457. Was King Karl's chieftain Rase
1 CONC borg As a brother-in-law to Erik Axelsson, he probably assisted in the overthrow of the state in 1457, at least he participated in the decisions that were implemented in the council shortly afterwards, but then King Kristian in 1463 demanded the op
1 CONC inion of the councilors about Jöns Bengtsson, he participated in all three decisions, which went out on his imprisonment. Sent together with others in 1464 to Danzig to summon King Charles again. Was present when Jöns Bengtsson was forced to la
1 CONC y down his worldly power in the fall of 1466 and was sent s. Oh. to Raseborg to persuade King Karl to return. After his death in 1470, he stood by Sten Sture's side. Lagman in Västmanland 1478-1486. Received Stegeborg castle and county 1487-09-03
1 CONC . Lagman in Uppland 1487 until his death. Lived 1494-02-00 21 , but was dead s. Oh. 22 , when succession was carried out after him 5/11 (according to the tombstone death 1493-03-23) 18 . Married 1st to Anna Johansdotter , died approx. 1453, daughte
1 CONC r of the knight and councilor Johan Nilsson Gädda and Elin Axelsdotter Brahe . Married 2nd shortly after 12/06/1455 to Ramborg Gustafsdotter , died 13/11/1492. Daughter of the knight and councilor Gustaf Ulfsson Sparre of Hjulsta and Ängsö and K
1 CONC ristina Folkadotter Rossviksätten who carried a Boat in the coat of arms.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT 1. Brita Gregersdotter , died before 1504-03-12 but after 1503-11-01 when she made a will. Buried in Krokek's monastery/E. Married 1468-10-24 (morning gift) to the knight, councilor and lawman in Södermanland Åke Jönsson ( Svarte Skåning ), t
1 CONC o Åkerö, in his 2nd marriage (married 1st 1445-01-18 to Mechtild Clausdotter ( Plata ), who was still alive in 1460), died in 1494.
1 CONT 1. Marina Gregersdotter , died in 1459, when she was inherited by her father.
1 CONT 2. Matthias Gregersson . Student in Greifswald 1487. Master there. 1490, then doctor decretorum. Enrolled at the University of Cologne 1492-09-07. Kanik in Uppsala. Provost in Strängnäs 1494-11-16. Bishop of Strängnäs 1501-08-27. Riksråd 1502
1 CONC . Stood on the side of the Sturars. Bequeathed to Denmark in 1504. Participated in the meetings in Malmö and Copenhagen in 1512 and 1513. Passed after Sten Sture's death in 1520 to King Kristian, but was beheaded. Oh. 8/11 in Stockholm's bloodbath
1 CONC , regardless he and the other councilors agreed to Kristian's adoption as king, and persuaded the common people to celebrate him and helped at his coronation. (SBL:23 p64 + p67; PhT 1951 p101; StrHm:1 p373, 455ff; OxoVasa p92f)
1 CONT 2. Bengt Gregersson . Knight and Councillor. Died before 1501. See Tab. 3.
1 CONT 2. Folke Gregersson . Knight and Councillor. Died 1507. See Tab. 4
0 @NFS5846@ NOTE === In 1446 he was living on Østby, Skjeberg ===
1 CONT In 1446 he was living on Østby, Skjeberg (ØF).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sigurds far, Sjøfar Rosensverd, synes å ha bodd på Østby fra ca. 1370. Han var i følge væbner i 1428, lagmann i Tønsberg 1429-38, og Borgartingslagmann i 1431 og 1438.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Den 28.03.1446 hadde han en tvist med væbneren Ture Karlsson og chorsbrødrene i Oslo angående gjerde og veihold på gården Vik, Skjeberg, som han eide en andel i. Sønnen Sjøfar møtte i sin fars ombud (DN II 769.)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Den hird de norske kongene hadde omgitt seg med, var på 1300-tallet i ferd med å forsvinne. Dette skyldtes til dels at den norske kongen ikke lenger oppholdt seg permanent i landet. Men vel så viktig var det at det hadde funnet sted en omformin
1 CONC g av den norske adelen. Hirden hadde vært inndelt i flere rangklasser med forskjellige privilegier. Fra slutten av Håkon 5.s regjeringstid (1299 - 1319) var det i virkeligheten bare tale om en tvedeling av det verdslige aristokratiet, i riddere o
1 CONC g væpnere. Lendmennene var i ferd med å dø ut, og nye ble ikke utnevnt. Likevel kom representantene for de gamle lendmannsættene ennå en tid til å spille en hovedrolle innen aristokratiet. Den norske adelen var med dette blitt mer lik den kon
1 CONC tinentale. Hedrende titulatur, hjelmer og våpenskjold var blitt vanlig blant norske stormenn. Sigurd hadde to sønner (minst): Sjøfar, til Østby, gift med Asbjørg Brynjulfsdatter. Nils, rådmann i Sarpsborg. Nils solgte i 1487 et halvt markebo
1 CONC l i Elgestad, Nøtterøy sammen med to av sønnene til Sjøfar, Brynjulf og Rolf. Brevet er datert Sarpsborg 29.01.1487 (DN XI 255).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Also:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sigurd Sjofarsen Rosensverd Lagmann was born about 1380 in of, Vik, Skjeberg, Ostfold. He died after Mar 28 1446. He has reference number 135824. !INFORMATION: Diplomatarium Norwegicum 1 p. 536, Ostfold Historielag Tidsskrift 
1 CONT b. 1 page 204. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT !INFORMATION: Hansen, Bent Billing and Vidar Billing Hansen, 
1 CONT "Rosensverdslektens Forfedre," Oslo, 1990, p. 85. "Sigurd Sjofarsen Rosensverd 
1 CONT (1380-....) Vaepner. Bosatt pa Vik i Skjeberg. Lagmann i Tonsberg og 
1 CONT Borgarsyssel. Gift med (Birgitte) Olufsdatter (1390-....)." (Sigurd Sjofarsen 
1 CONT Rosensverd (1380-....) Esquire. Resident (Lord?) of Vik in [the parish of] 
1 CONT Skjeberg. Magistrate in [the parish of] Tonsberg [in the county of Vestfold] 
1 CONT and Borgarsyssel [in an unidentified location. He married (Birgitte) 
1 CONT Olufsdatter (1390-....).) 
1 CONT 
1 CONT !INFORMATION: S. Otto Brenner, "Nachkommen Gorms den Alten" (Stuttgart: 
1 CONT Silberburg-Verlag, 1965). 
1 CONT p. 2636. "N.N. Olavsdatter (Gyldenhorn); m. spatestens (at the latest) 1433 
1 CONT Sigurd Sjorfarsson (Rosensverd), Knappe (Esquire) 1428, Lagmann in Tonsberg u. 
1 CONT in Borgsyssel 1429-38, d. fruhstehens (at the earliest) 28 Mar 1446, S. d. 
1 CONT Sjofar (Rolvsson) (Rosensverd) in Ostby (1370)."
1 CONT 
1 CONT Noted events in his life were:
1 CONT • Occupation. væbner, lagmann.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sigurd married Birgitte Olafsdatter Gyldenhorn, daughter of Olaf Thorstensen Gyllenhorn and Aase Ulvsdatter, before 1433. (Birgitte Olafsdatter Gyldenhorn was born circa 1390 in Elingaard, Onsøy, Østfold, Norway.)
