0 @NFS5857@ NOTE === Linage Role ===
1 CONT Ingeborg Karlsdotter Lejonbalk (also spelled Ingborg), born approximately 1245 in Simonstorp, Östergötland, Sweden, married Ulf Karlsson (Ulv) from the Folkungaätten Ulv branch and was the mother of Filip Ulfsson (Ulv) (born circa 1265).��Fa
1 CONC mily ConnectionsDaughter of Karl Ingeborgsson Lejonbalk, she belonged to the Lejonbalk (lion beam) noble family, with siblings including Katarina Karlsdotter Lejonbalk (who married into Puke) and others like Filip and Folke Karlsson Lejonbalk. He
1 CONC r union brought estates and the lion heraldry into the Ulv line, elevating their status among 13th-century frälsemän.��Lineage RoleThis marriage produced the Tillbakaseende Ulv descendants, including Staffan Ulfsson (Ulv) and Kristina Staffan
1 CONC sdotter Ulv (born circa 1375), who wed Bengt Uddsson Vinstorpaätten—directly tying to the Vinstorpa, Rödbjälke, Grip, and Kafle-Vinge ancestry ending at Ingeborg Johansdotter Kafle (1462).� She died around 1287–1319, per user trees durin
1 CONC g Folkunga consolidation.�
