0 @NFS5871@ NOTE ===  Since there may be some confusion betwe ===
1 CONT  Since there may be some confusion between Anund and Amund,information on both brothers is given here. Anund  (brother of Amund) inherited land in Østre Holter fromhis father and he inherited equally from his mother. He sold apart, 8 ertogbøl, t
1 CONC o Geileik of Holum in Ullensaker. Gudbrand ofHolter who married Jon Ketilsdotter may have gotten that part.There was a dispute about it in 1347. Their son Amund was calledAmund Lagabjørnsson in 1347 in the legal case about 8 ertogbølin Østre (Ea
1 CONC st) Holter farm. He was also listed in that decadeas Amund Kampe who when he gave 1 øyresbøl of land in Holter tothe Nes church group and a like amount to Fenstad church.  As aminimum, Nes, Fenstad and Udnes churches were in the group. About 133
1 CONC 0 he was mentioned as Anund, not Amund, Holtakampe, whoKåre Amundsson had inherited land from in Nedre (North)Holter.This was in relation to a case where one Torbjørn hadsummoned Kåre on behalf of his stepdaughter, MargreteEiriksdotter. In 129
1 CONC 9 there was an Anund, who died before then,who was called a mother's brother (uncle) to Herr GudleikKristinsson. The mother of Gudleik was Kristin BjørnsdotterKamp. Anund had sold 4 øyresbøl of land in Holter to Gunnar, apeasant salt man, who di
1 CONC dn't own any land because of the highdemand due to much church ownership of land at the time. Anundhad made an agreement but had not carried it out. Gunnar claimedthat the agreement should require Gudleik to give him 4 øyresbolin Frogner farm, an
1 CONC d Gudleik should make up for land he had lostin Holter after Anund died. Herr Gudleik of Holter gave 3øyresbol of Katterud farm to the Nes church group and 1øyresbbøl in North Holter was given to Fenstad church for thesalvation of Anund Gudleiks
1 CONC son's soul. He was surely a son ofGudleik Kristensson, and named after his mother's brother. Amund Bjørnsson married NN (no known first name) Haftorsdotterand had the following children: Bjørne who married Gro Torleifsdotter. Kåre who married Å
1 CONC shild, and was mentio ned in the court caseabove. Eystein who married Margrete Eiriksdotter. He was known asEystein Kampasson and died before 1330. He gave 1 øyresbøl ofland in Kårud to Nes church group and Pål of Holter gave a likeamount. Erla
1 CONC nd, mentioned in 1327-29 as guiding Kussevåpen (farm?). Alsorecorded as Baron Erling Amundsen. Bård of Kussevåpen (DN I 189, DN II 171) Pål, who had also given land to Nes church group. Arne who lived in 1347 but was dead before 1357.
