0 @NFS5885@ NOTE === Noble history  ===
1 CONT Ulf Filipsson (Ulv), born approximately 1300 in Valkebo, Östergötland, Sweden, was a Swedish knight and royal official who served as ståthållare (governor) in Skåne from 1333, auditing customs at Skanör and Falsterbo under King Magnus Eriksso
1 CONC n ��.Family LineageSon of riksråd Filip Ulfsson (Ulv) and NN Karlsdotter, he married a daughter of Staffan Röriksson (Staffanssönernas ätt) and fathered Staffan Ulfsson (Ulv) (born before 1348), whose daughter Kristina Staffansdotter Ulv we
1 CONC d Bengt Uddsson Vinstorpaätten, linking directly to the Vinstorpa chain ��.Noble CareerDied by 1350, Ulf held estates at Vinäs (Gammalkil) and lands across Östergötland, Småland, and Södermanland, exemplifying Tillbakaseende Ulv clan's ri
