0 @NFS5895@ NOTE ===  It is said that Bothild of Hvam was "pe ===
1 CONT  It is said that Bothild of Hvam was "perhaps the daughter toHerr Gudleik. She did give 1 øyresbol of Østre Holter farm toNes church , Gudleik was named after his mother Kristin Bjørnsdatter Kamp ofMellom Holter instead of his father, Jon Holtes
1 CONC son.This mayindicate that the Kamp family had higher standing than the Holtefamily. He was a knight by 1299, and addressed as Herr Gudleik. Gudleik Kristinessøn was mentioned in a February 25, 1299lawsuit document between he and Gunnar Bonde Saltk
1 CONC arl. Gudleikwas identified as the nephew of Anund who had died. Anund hadsold 4 øyresbol in Holter farm with security in Biertnes farm toGunnar who had never received property rights to it. The suitconcluded with an agreement where Herr Gudleik sh
1 CONC ould turn overto Gunnar 4 øyresbol in Store Frogner farm and pay him rent forthe lost land in Holter since Anund died. Herr Gudleik of Holter farm gave 3 øyresbol in Katterud farm inNes and 1 øyresbol in Nedre Holter farm to Nes church for Anund
1 CONC Gudleiksson' soul. He is likely a son of Gudleik named after hisuncle.
