0 @NFS5922@ NOTE === Om Ulf Karlsson ===
1 CONT "Vapen: vingad pilspets. Nämnes tidigast 1276, då han vid fredsmötet vid Göta älv var en av de fyra världsliga stormän som tillsammans med fyra biskopar skulle representera konung Magnus Ladulås. Han hade då ännu ej den på riddarvärdigh
1 CONC et tydande herrtitel med vilken han kan beläggas först 1280. Ågde "Akasrö”, möjligen i Oppunda hd i Södermanland, och kvarnar i Torshälla i samma landskap. " Adelsvapen-Wiki, Tillbakaseende ulv
0 @NFS5923@ NOTE === SOURCE: ===
1 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Karlsson-944
1 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Tillbakaseende_ulv#TAB_10
1 CONT go to 2 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ulf Karlsson probably born in 1247 or 1248, † 1281 and buried in Skänninge. Weapon: Winged Arrowhead. First mentioned in 1276, when he was one of the four worldly magnates who, together with four bishops, were to represent King Magnus Ladulås a
1 CONC t the peace meeting at Göta river . He did not yet have the lordly title indicating knighthood, with which he can only be invested in 1280. Ågde "Akasrö", possibly in Oppunda hd in Södermanland, and mills in Torshälla in the same province. Pos
1 CONC sibly married to a daughter of the lawman in Tiohärad Karl Ingeborgason Lejonbalk .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ingeborg Ulfsdotter , † between 1297 and 1307. Married to the knight Knut Matsson Lejonbjälke , who is first mentioned in 1280, became a lawman in Närke between 1279 and 1283 and a councilor at the latest in 1288 and died in 1289. She was remar
1 CONC ried in 1296 to the knight and the councilor, later the dukes Eriks and Valdemars drots Abjörn Sixtensson Sparre of Tofta .
1 CONT Philippus Ulfsson , 1296-1333, knight, councillor. See tab. 3.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ulf Karlsson Vingad Strale  
1 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Karlsson-944
1 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulf_Karlsson_(Ulv)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ulf Karlsson (Ulv) , probably born in 1247 or 1248, died in 1281 , knight , Swedish councilor and for a time Sweden's first prince . Progenitor of the Ulv family . He was the son of Karl Karlsson (Ulv) . Seal weapon : winged beam (arrowhead).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ulf Karlsson was a cousin of King Magnus Ladulås and known as one of his most important men. He was present in 1276 at the peace meeting at the Göta river where he was appointed Sweden's first prince :
1 CONT 
1 CONT From the time of King Magnus Ladulå , three men are known to have held the office of duke. Ulf Karlsson was drots in 1276, Knut Matsson , whose name we find under the Scanning Charter with the attached title: drotset 1280 and Magnus Ragvaldsson 12
1 CONC 88.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Possibly married to a daughter of the lawman in Tiohärad Karl Ingeborgasson (Lejonbalk) .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children
1 CONT Margareta Ulfsdotter
1 CONT Filip Ulfsson (Wolf)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sources 
1 CONT The Folkungaätten in Carl Georg Starbäck and Per Olof Bäckström , Stories from Swedish history (1885-1886), First volume. The fairy tale age. The Middle Ages. I. To the Kalmare Union.
1 CONT Svea Rike's Council length
1 CONT adelsvapen.com: Looking back wolf
