0 @NFS5973@ NOTE === from Wikipedia and Adelsvapen ===
1 CONT Bo Nilsson ( Night and Day ) , died no earlier than 1322, was a Swedish magnate of the Night and Day family. Son of Nils Sigridsson and married to Cecilia Knutsdotter (Aspenäsätten) .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Biography 
1 CONT Bo Nilsson was a lawman in Östergötland's law saga in 1318 and one of the followers of dukes Erik and Valdemar . In 1319 he was a councilor also with Duke Erik's son, King Magnus Eriksson . Was one of the 7 lawmen who signed the Charter of Freedo
1 CONC m in 1319 [ 1 ] . Bo Nilsson was one of the signatories of the association in Skara in 1322 and seems to have died not long afterwards.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Family 
1 CONT Nilsson married Cecilia Knutsdotter (Aspenäsätten) . Together they had the children: [ 2 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ingeborg Bosdotter, married in 1328 to Johan Tomasson (Grip, older family) . Married the second time to the knight Johan Dansson .
1 CONT Benkt Bosson, 1357 district chief in Skärkind's district .
1 CONT Magnus Bosson, lived in 1336.
1 CONT Bo Bosson (Night and Day) , knight and councillor.
1 CONT Ragnborg Bosdotter, lived in 1336.
1 CONT Elena Bosdotter, was included in 1336 in St. Martin's monastery in Skänninge.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT References 
1 CONT Night and Day, 1. Bo Nilsson in Nordic Family Book (second edition, 1913)
1 CONT Family tree Night and Day family
1 CONT "Night and Day No. 13 - Adelsvapen-Wiki" . www.adelsvapen.com . Read October 12, 2017 .
1 CONT Notes 
1 CONT ^ Bo Niclison legifer osgocie ; 1319 on July 8 (Sd 2199).
1 CONT ^ Schlegel, Bernhard ; Carl Arvid Klingspor (1875). The one granted with letters of shield but not to the House of Knights introduced the family tables of the Swedish nobility . Stockholm: PA Norstedt & Söner. page 290. Libris 19655314
1 CONT Further reading 
1 CONT Liedgren, Jan:  Bo Nilsson (Night and Day) in Swedish Biographical Lexicon (1987-1989)
