0 @NFS5990@ NOTE === Critical Notes on Erik Sigurdsen Galte ===
1 CONT Norwegian historians and genealogists have been debating the history of the Torsnes people for nearly 100 years, with arguments dating back to at least Solleid (1930), who theorized that the owners of Torsnes descend from Gaut på Ænes/Mel. New re
1 CONC search starting in the 1950s, however, offer an alternative theory. Dahl (1950), for example, uses a 1409 diploma (DN XXI, #249) to argue that the ancestry of the Torsnes people can be traced to Viking på Torsnes (c1190- ) and his daughter Inga Vi
1 CONC kingsdatter. As far as I can tell, most Norwegian researchers have shifted to Dahl’s theory, including Losnegård (2003), who wrote the bygdebok for Jondal kommune.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Neither theory contests the claim that Erik Sigurdsen is the son of Sigurd Torsnes (whether it be Sigurd Guttormsen [the likely case] or Sigurd Gautsen [now less likely]. And research has uncovered the following, which I have used to 'clean up' th
1 CONC e familysearch records (duplicates, etc). 
1 CONT 
1 CONT He had two wives, whose names we do no know. From the first marriage we have Gaut Eriksen (the famous Baron) and Olov Eriksdatter; from the second, Gyrid Eriksdatter. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Early theories (Høyland 1939) proposed that he married Elin(e) Toraldsdatter Kane. Current research suggests this is not the case. While I have kept that 'marriage', I have shifted the children to their respective NN mothers. Perhaps in future w
1 CONC e may find out the 'truth' for certain. Please see the Torsnes document in Memories for additional discussion
