0 @NFS6032@ NOTE === Source: ===
1 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Bagge_af_Berga_nr_118#TAB_3
1 CONT 
1 CONT Noble family Bagge af Berga no. 118
1 CONT Ancient family of salvation. Renovation of old nobility 1517-02-29. Introduction 1642. Extinct in 1955.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Extinct on the sword side 1969-07-14, on the spin side 1963-04-10.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Lowercase. pedigree. with nobility the Bagge af Söderby , Gyllensparre , Forstenasläkten and Ulfana families .
1 CONT 
1 CONT The coat of arms of a sparrow over a leaf was worn in the Middle Ages by several more or less fringed families. Freedom G. Djurklou, who in an essay in Historik tidskrift for the year 1891 dealt with these families, named them Eskilssönner, Lindor
1 CONC mssönner, Abjörnssönner and Häggassönner after the first names of the progenitors. The largest of these families was that of Abjörnssönern, of which the Bagge af Berga and Bagge af Söderby families are undoubtedly a direct continuation on t
1 CONC he sword side. The progenitor Abjörn Nockesson brought in his seal a six-pointed star, as well as with some changes also the son Jöns Abjörnsson to approx. in 1390, when the latter adopted the mother's shield the spar over a leaf. She belonged t
1 CONC o the family of the sons of Lindorms, which a few years later probably ended on the side of the sword. At the time of its introduction, the coat of arms of the Baggeätterna was slightly changed, in that the right support of the spar was doubled. H
1 CONC owever, this doubling occurs exceptionally in the seals of some family members already in the latter half of the 16th century. From the family of the Abjörnssons also descend on the paternal side the noble family no. 146 Gyllensparre, and on the m
1 CONC aternal side the noble families no. 2 Forstena family and no. 153 Ulfana, all of whom use the spar over a leaf as a shield.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT TABLE 1
1 CONT Abjörn Nockesson , (oversight tab1), issues letter 1344-01-02. Married before the said year to N . N.​ Lindormsdotter , who in the coat of arms passed the spar over a blade.
