0 @NFS6041@ NOTE === source: ===
1 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sparre_av_Tofta
1 CONT 
1 CONT TABLE 2
1 CONT Abjörn Sixtensson (son of Sixten, tab. 1). Appears in the records from 1295, probably already a knight, certainly in 1296. Was councilor in 1297. Mentioned as duke Eriks drots from 1302 and from 1307 also as duke Valdemars. Between 17.5 1304 and 8
1 CONC .1 1307, he disappeared from the Swedish diploma material due to exile and confiscation of goods. Died 1310. Owned Salsta in Lena sn in Norunda hd in Uppland and Ängsö in the same name sn in Yttertjurbo hd in Västmanland. Was married in 1296 t
1 CONC o Ingeborg Ulfsdotter, daughter of the knight Ulf Karlsson ( Wolf ) and widow of the knight Knut Matsson, who was apparently a lawman in Närke as early as 1282, is mentioned as a councilor in 1288 and died in 1289. Mrs. Ingeborg, who owned estate
1 CONC s in Kinds, Kåkinds, Vadsbo and Vartofta hd in Västergötland and in Karlstads and ölme hd i Värmland, died in 1307. In addition to the sons listed below, Mr. Abjörn had a daughter Ingeborg, who was probably born in an illegitimate relationshi
1 CONC p, which Mr. Abjörn entered into before his marriage to Mrs. Ingeborg. He gave this illegitimate daughter the same year he died, 1310, a substantial gift with the consent of his mother and his sister Kristina, all in accordance with what was stipu
1 CONC lated in the Östgöta law's inheritance code regarding gifts to frill children. If Ingeborg had been born in wedlock, it is inconceivable that neither she nor her husband, as the relationship was with the brothers' other half-sister Birgitta, woul
1 CONC d ever be found as a guarantor of the Abjörnsons' many business transactions. As an illegitimate child, Ingeborg, on the other hand, did not belong to the family, even though she was recognized. She was certainly still alive in 1343, possibly as l
1 CONC ate as 1351. Was at least from 1310 married to Master Herman in Kavlebäck in Västra Ny sn in Aska hd in Östergötland, who was still alive in 1320. Ingeborg owned estates in Åsunda hd in Uppland as well as in Aska, Dals and Göstrings HD in Ös
1 CONC tergötland.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sons:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Nils Abjörnsson, 1317, died 1359, knight, councillor, lawman, drots. See tab. 3 .
1 CONT Ulf Abjörnsson, 1317, died 1347 or 1348, knight, councillor, lawman. See tab. 4 .
