0 @NFS6069@ NOTE === Person cited using information below validates this person ===
1 CONT  The relevant article in the same volume is Thomle’s “Den saakaldte familie Bratt i Gudbrandsdalen” (pp. 97–122, with corrections/additions on pp. 260–264). This does document Guttorm Endridsen of Bjølstad as a real historical squire/lan
1 CONC downer in Gudbrandsdalen (Bjølstad farm, Heidal/Sel area) in the late 1400s–early 1500s, with his son Øystein Guttormsen Bratt. The article treats the Bratt line as a documented (if sometimes “so-called”) gentry family tied to specific farm
1 CONC s. Your tree’s dates (Guttorm 1437–1530; Øystein ~1475–1550) align with the long lifespan and activity range described there.
1 CONT •  Verdict on the note: It does not directly validate any ancestor in your tree (wrong page/article). However, the Bratt article in NST vol. 2 does provide legitimate scholarly backing for the 1437–1530 Guttorm segment—stronger than most 15th
1 CONC -century gentry links.
