0 @NFS6143@ NOTE === Source: ===
1 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Lillie_af_Greger_Mattssons_%C3%A4tt_nr_6
1 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matts_%C3%96dgislason_(Lillie)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Matts Ödgislason (Lillie) , born around 1380, died 2 August 1442 , was a Swedish savior, councilor and lawman in Södermanland's law saga . The statement that he should have been a knight is incorrect.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Biography
1 CONT Matts was the son of Ödgisl Sunason and Ramborg Staffansdotter ( Ulv ). The father bore the same coat of arms as the family of the Liquid Sons . In 1383 or 1384 the father died when Matts was probably still very young. Only after the year 1400 doe
1 CONC s he appear as an adult, as district chief in Selebo district in 1410, a post his grandfather was the last known former holder of, although last held in 1366. Probably before March 1413 and certainly before May 1416, he married Ingeborg Gregersdott
1 CONC er ( The aspen ridges ). Between 1412 and 1416 he also inherited Lagnö from his mother. [ 3 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT When the bishop of Strängnäs, at the behest of Erik of Pomerania in 1413-1414, carried out the raefsteting, Matts was one of the bysitters, as was his mother-in-law's brother Nils Eringislason , lawman in Södermanland. He appears to have becom
1 CONC e a councilor in the late 1420s and attended most council meetings during the Engelbrecht Rebellion . In 1437 he seems to have been the one assigned the task of negotiating with rebellious valley men; the ensuing meeting in Enköping led to a settl
1 CONC ement. [ 3 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Matt's wife's niece Katarina Karlsdotter (Gumsehuvud) married the marshal Karl Knutsson (Bonde) in 1438, and from at least this time Matts was a follower of him, and among other things got to take over Gästrikland, which had previously been grante
1 CONC d to Kristiern Nilsson (Vasa) when, a few days after the wedding, Karl became the head of state . Even before Nils Erengislason died in 1440, Matts had to take over his lawman office. When Karl Knutsson and Kristiern Nilsson were reconciled in th
1 CONC e fall of 1441, Matts was one of the king's six pledges , as well as one of the sworn men when in the same spring of 1442 he was accused of having caused the death of Peder Ulvsson (Roos) and acquitted himself with the oath of twelve men . In 1442
1 CONC , King Karl had to transfer Turku Castle to King Kristofer of Bavaria and Mats became a courtier there a few months before his death. [ 3 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Matts was buried in Riddarholm church, where later also the son Gregers was buried. [ 3 ]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT ^ Matts Ödgislason (Lillie) , Swedish Biographical Lexicon , Swedish Biographical Lexicon ID : 10309 , read online . [source from Wikidata]
1 CONT ^ [ a b c d e f g ] Gustaf Elgenstierna , The introduced genealogies of the Swedish nobility , vol. 4, Norstedts förlag , 1928, p. 663, read: 17 January 2023. [source from Wikidata]
1 CONT ^ [ a b c d ] Hans Gillingstam :  Matts Ödgislason (Lillie) in Swedish Biographical Lexicon (1981)
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Matts Ödgislesson , to Lagnö. Brought a lily in the coat of arms. Sealed the mother's renewal letter 1384-08-02 to the father's gift of Hornstäve to Vadstena monastery and her deed of sale to her cousin the knight Sten Bengtsson to land in Norrl
1 CONC änna in Länna parish, Södermanland county, which she inherited from her mother. Was a squire in 1411. Holder of the Räfstetingsdom in Södermanland in 1413 and 1414. Was district chief in Selebo district in 1418 and again in 1440. Signed amon
1 CONC g the council letters to Norway and the German estates about King Erik's deposition in 1434. Knight. Was lawman in Södermanland 1440-10-03 and governor at Turku Castle in 1442. Died there probably s. Oh. certainly before 19/9) 17 and buried in th
1 CONC e gray monk monastery in Stockholm. Married probably before 1413-03-08 and certainly before 1416-05-08 to Ingeborg Gregersdotter , lived 1459-08-15, when she was seriously ill and probably died in the summer of å., daughter of the knight Greger Be
1 CONC ngtsson (Aspenäsätten. The name "Blå-ätten" is obsolete), and Catharina Erengisledotter (Hammerstaätten. The name "Night and Day in the long run" is obsolete). (SBL:23 p62f; SD no.1236; HTF:1964 p12)
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Anna Mattsdotter . Was a nun in Vårfruberga monastery 1442-06-15.
1 CONT Greg Mattsson . Knight and Councillor. Died 1495. See Tab. 2
1 CONT Ramborg Mattsdotter , died in 1451 and buried in Vadstena monastery church, where her tombstone is found 18 . Married 1st 1426-02-27 to the knight and councilor and chieftain of Axvall Bo Knutsson (grip head), died 1442 or shortly thereafter. Marri
1 CONC ed 2nd to the knight and councilor and chieftain Eggert Albrektsson Krummedik in his 1st marriage (married 2nd to Marina Jönsdotter, who lived as a widow in 1491), died 1487 18 .
1 CONT Clara Mattsdotter , died unmarried before 19 1463-05-18.
1 CONT Bengta 20 Mattsdotter , died 1452 20 . Married before 1444-08-01 to the knight, the Riksdag and Riksfänder Erik Axelsson (Tott) , to Lagnö, in his 1st marriage [married 2nd before 1455-06-12, probably already in the summer or autumn of 1453 1
1 CONC 8 , to Elin Gustafs daughter in her 2nd marriage (married 1st to the knight, councilor and lawman Knut Stensson Bielke af Åkerö , died 1451), lived 1494-07-15 but died 1496-06-02, daughter of the knight and councilor Gustaf Algotsson (Sture), t
1 CONC o Ängsö and Lagmansö, and his 2nd wife Märta Ulfsdotter (Sparre )], died shortly before 28-03-1481.
