0 @NFS6148@ NOTE === https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A4dda%C3%A4tten ===
1 CONT Gädda was a Småland way of life , known from the latter half of the 14th century and extinct in 1508.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Coat of arms: The family carried a so-called talking coat of arms in the form of a pike in the coat of arms.
1 CONT Gädda was formerly believed to be descended from Sven Trottason, who carried two crossed pearls in his coat of arms. At the end of the 14th century, Nils Gädda belonged to the aristocratic party fighting against Magnus Eriksson and Håkan Magnuss
1 CONC on . At the beginning of the 15th century, his son, the squire Karl Gädda, held Broby in Östergötland and Lars Gädda was canon in Linköping .
1 CONT 
1 CONT Karl Gädda was married to an unnamed daughter of the knight Karl Öra . Their sons were the councilor Jon, or Johan Gädda (died in the 1450s) and Erengisle Gädda , who took part in the civil wars of the 1450s and 1460s on opposite sides.
