0 @NFS6231@ NOTE ===  Han hadde sønene: 1. Sigurd n. 1333, 2. ===
1 CONT  Han hadde sønene: 1. Sigurd n. 1333, 2. Aslak, 3. Berdor n . 1357-1370 Korleis Alv på Sigerstad i 1334 og Kolbein på F lesberg i 1333 måtte vere beslekta er ikkje sikkert. Men de i førde begge det same  Bolt-våpenet som Hr Håkon Ogmundsso n
1 CONC , ridder og riksråd i 1309-1346.
0 @NFS6232@ NOTE === Who Was Elin Ivarsdatter? ===
1 CONT Evidence for Erik Sigurdsen marrying an Elin Ivarsdatter doesn't seem to exist. If there was such a person, she would have been Erik Sigurdsen's 2nd cousin, born a generation after him (or something like that--based on the the Gaut Unge descent the
1 CONC ory advanced by Høyland 1939).  Based on research by various Norwegian genealogists & historians, she doesn't appear as Erik's wife (Høyland 1939; Roskildehistorie, n.d.). 
1 CONT 
1 CONT I'm leaving both relationships for now. Note that only two children would come from his first marriage (to whichever Elin!): Gaute Eriksen and Olov Eriksdatter. Gyrid is likely Erik's daughter from his second wife, whose name we do not know.
1 CONT 
1 CONT For more information, see 'Sunnhordlandsetter' (adapted from 1939 article by Rasmus Høyland and augmented with further research): https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/Sunnhordlands%C3%A6tter#Galt%C3%A6tta
1 CONT 
1 CONT And "Galtung," a proposed pedigree for the Galtung and related families: https://www.roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/Galtung/Galtung.htm
