0 @NFS6251@ NOTE === Picture on page 25 of the Anders Rustad  ===
1 CONT Picture on page 25 of the Anders Rustad Book
1 CONT 
1 CONT (from the Anders Rustad Ættebok of 1948, translated by Richard Flisrand) After Henrik Miltzow had gone through school in Bergen, he also studied in Copenhagen, Edinburgh, and Rostok, and in 1622 he became a lecturer at the Latin school in Bergen
1 CONC .  The 31st of August, 1623 he became the parish priest at Voss. He was only 24 years old, and remained in Voss until his death.  In 1642 he became head pastor for Handanger.  In 1645, he was selected the representative for the Bergen area, to a co
1 CONC nference at Akershus called by Hannibal Sehested. In 1649, Henrik Miltzow bought the Lydvo farm of his former wife, Kirsten.     He founded the "Vangens Poorhouse for Widows", or Voss Widow's Home", as it is now known.  He also built a "Kjerringast
1 CONC ova", the Women's building, which later was enlarged and became, the Voss Misjonshotell.  This burned in the bombing of Voss in April of 1940. The Voss Church was repaired in his time, paid partly by him.  The old picture Bible in the sacristy of t
1 CONC he Voss Church, printed in 1589, was (commissioned? "kostet han innbinding") in 1664.     According to the memorial plaque in the Voss Church, he and his wife Kristine were buried under the choir floor in the church.
0 @NFS6252@ NOTE ===  (1599) ===
1 CONT  (1599)
0 @NFS6253@ NOTE === Christense/Madsen * ===
1 CONT Christense/Madsen *
0 @NFS6254@ NOTE === He ended his schooling in Bergen, and co ===
1 CONT He ended his schooling in Bergen, and continued his studies in Copenhagen (started here in 1619), Edinburgh and Rostock(started here in 1621). Returned to Bergen in 1622. Was elected sogneprest at an age of 25 years old on 31 aug 1623, and electe
1 CONC d provst for Hardanger Provsti in 1642. Elected as "deputerest" for "Bergen stifts prester" by statholder Hannibal Sehested.
1 CONT 
1 CONT He was a very rich man, and gave of his great wealth to restore a church and donated money to a place for widows. He gathered a lot of money and property.
