0 @NFS6261@ NOTE === Who was 'Eline Toraldsdatter Kane'? ===
1 CONT Trees based on older research have this Eline Toraldsdatter as the wife of Erik Sigurdsen Torsnes. Recent research indicates Erik Sigurdsen had two NN wives and three children between the two: NN1, Gaute (gm??? but no children) & Olav (gm Viking To
1 CONC rgilsen); NN2, Guri (gm Gunnar Kane). Thus, if she did exist, her marriage to Erik Sigurdsen appears highly speculative (as much of early Medieval era Norwegian genealogical research is), if not fictive. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT If she is one of the wives of Erik Sigurdsen, it's logical to assume a birth in the 1310s, and a death in the 1340s--or earlier. But then she is not the mother of Gyrid 'Guri' Eriksdatter. But note that almost all the dates for people from the Medi
1 CONC eval era are estimates, speculation, etc.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Additionally, there is definitely no evidence she would have had a marriage to a Viking Sigurdsen, with two children (in fact, whoever put that into FS creates an erroneous circular kink in the tree). 
1 CONT 
1 CONT See Harstad, 2014, whose articled is excerpted at https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/Askegodset_p%C3%A5_Moster%C3%B8y_i_Rogaland)
