0 @NFS6344@ NOTE === Guttorm Kalvsen ===
1 CONT Guttorm Kalvsen is the only known child of Inga Vikingsdatter Torsnes og Kalv på Tornes. Little is known about Guttorm in terms of historical documentation; his full name appears in a 1409 diploma, where his descendants Bård og Guttorm Sigurdse
1 CONC n receive testimony confirming their ancestry and thus their noble timber rights in Knarrevik Forest (DN XXI, #249, dated 1409 at Talgje i Ryfylke): “All men who see or hear this letter send Viking Eirikson, Aslak Torkelson, Ketil Erlandson, Viki
1 CONC ng Gudleikson, Gunnar Askjellson and Tore Sigurdson, noblemen of God and theirs, greetings, as they make it known that we know to be true what our fathers told us and likewise the oldest men who lived in Varaldsøy skiprede and Jondal parish, and h
1 CONC ave heard nothing else, except that the Torsnesmen, one after the other who are mentioned here: Viking and Inga, his daughter, Guttorm Kalvson (her son) and Sigurd Guttormson, Guttorm Sigurdson, Sigurd Guttormson, Bård and Guttorm Sigurdsønner, o
1 CONC wn and have owned the Knarrevik forest out to the gorge at Årsand and into Årvik ... between mountain and fjord as eternal property, one after the other as we have mentioned before. We the aforesaid courtiers have never heard of herding or mentio
1 CONC ned that the Torsnesmenne gave (“guldo”) or sold to anyone, but that each, one after the other, has inherited the aforementioned forest Knarrevik, which is located in the parish of Ænes and Varaldsøy skiprede in Sunnhordland, and in true test
1 CONC imony of this we put our seals to this letter which was set up on Thursday the first day of summer in the 20th year of the reign of our lord Eirik with God’s grace Norway king”.
1 CONT 
1 CONT No additional information is known, except what is speculative (which should be treated very skeptically without research-based documentation and explanation).
