0 @NFS6424@ NOTE === !A book, Title, "SOREN HERMAN NELSON AND ===
1 CONT !A book, Title, "SOREN HERMAN NELSON AND MARY CHRISTENA PETERSEN HISTORY, ANCESTORS AND DESCENDANTS" written by L Don Berchtold, published in 1999 by Berchtold Publishing Company, Limited Edition, Copies in the Family History Library of The LDS Chu
1 CONC rch in Salt Lake City. See Source Material under Berchtold.  Data taken from the IGI.
0 @NFS6425@ NOTE === Rootsweb notes ===
1 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=sak42&id=I1326
1 CONT Reference Number: 191
1 CONT _UID: C4EEB457DB8EDD4DB27D8A525BE251EBD49A
1 CONT 
1 CONT Kristen Jensson was probably of Danish origin. By 1566, he was a
1 CONT squire in the household of the Bergenhus governor, Erik Rosenkranz.
1 CONT Kristen became the Royal Bailiff (fut) for the county of Sogn and
1 CONT operated under the governor's authority. He married the widow of the
1 CONT previous bailiff and took up the office sometime around 1567. At that
1 CONT time a Royal Bailiff was practically a personal retainer of the
1 CONT governor and his fate was closely linked to that of the governor.
1 CONT Whenever a governor died or resigned his office, there was a general
1 CONT changeover in the ranks of the Royal Bailiffs. Erik Rosenkranz
1 CONT resigned his office in Aun 1568 and returned to Denmark. Kristen, who
1 CONT had married a Norwegian noblewoman, elected to remain in Norway,
1 CONT although he was undoubtedly replaced in office by a retainer of the
1 CONT new governor. It is known that Kristen was no longer a Royal Bailiff
1 CONT in 1574 when he mortgaged some property. In that document he signed
1 CONT himself "til Kaupanger", an indication that he was a member of the
1 CONT nobility and probably had his setegård at Kaupanger. He also used the
1 CONT same title in 1595. Although he doesn't appear to have held any
1 CONT official office after 1568, it is probable that Kristen lived the life
1 CONT of a wealthy and prominent landowner at Kaupanger until he died
1 CONT sometime between 1595 and 1599.
