0 @NFS6431@ NOTE === Who Is Sigrid Bårdsdatter? ===
1 CONT Historical research based on primary sources (etc.) indicates that Sigurd Guttormsen Torsnes married a Sigrid Guttormsdatter (not Bårdsdatter). This includes the 1306 resettlement DN II, #81) of her father's estate, which proves her patronym was G
1 CONC uttormsdatter. And a 1326 will (DN II, #169), that proves Sigurd's wife's name was Sigrid (she was left a bequest of a scarlet cloak with white leather trim by Magnhild Ketilsdatter; and her sister-in-law, Ingebjørd, who was the wife of Sigurd's b
1 CONC rother Nikolas, was also given a bequest). So, 'Sigrid Bardsdatter' is Sigrid Guttormsdatter.
