0 @NFS6454@ NOTE ===  Gisle Semmingsen was manager of Garvik  ===
1 CONT  Gisle Semmingsen was manager of Garvik in North Odal as recordedin the tax records from 1593-1605. In 1608 he was at Haug inNorth Odal and was involved in a court case in the division ofMiddle Garvik and Austvatn. This may have been a little after
1 CONC 1605 that he, in his older days, was manager of Haug after hisson, Nils, who went to Runni in Nes. The division of the estateof Vågstad in Nes was on March 13, 1635 following the deaths ofGisle Semmingsen and his wife, Toruana Ottersdatter. Linde
1 CONC r inNorth Odal was given to Otter Seim's children, but it wasalready in pawn. That may have been the Gisle Haug who went toVågstad in his older years. Already in 1567 Gisle Semmingsen inOdalen was recorded. He lived until about 1635 and must haveb
1 CONC een very old, but he could also have died several years beforethe division was concluded. Gisle was still manager of Haug in1615 and owned 25 lispund in Haug, 10 lispund in Auli in SouthOdal, 10 lispund in Garvik, and 5 lispund in Seim. Theirchildr
1 CONC en were: VIa. Semming, who was manager of Middle Vågstad according torecords of 1543 to about 1640, and owned 10 lispund in Vågstadand 5 lispund in Lier in 1615. (Note: A different SemmingGislesen  than our direct ancestor.) VIb. Nils, who was ma
1 CONC nager of Haug in North Odal according torecords of 1593-1605 and part of Runni in Nes and owned 10lispund in Middle Vågstad in 1615. VIc. Otter, who managed Seim in South Odal, and who owned 2 1/2lispund in Skarning in Nes and married Rønnaug an
1 CONC d whosechildren were: Kristoffer, manager of Garvik. Amund, manager ofFalla in Fet. Gunner, manager of Huser in Nes. Mari, married toØyen in South Odal. Marit, married to Vestby in South Odal. VId. Mari married Embret Tostensen of Upper Valstad i
1 CONC n Nes whoowned 11 lispund in Upper Valstad, 10 lispund in Middle Vågstad,2 1/2 lispund in Jaelberg in Nannestad, and 1 1/2 lispund inBreen in Nes in 1615. Eline's death was recorded in 1651. (Her brothers-in-law werePal Berg in Udnes, Ole Auli i
1 CONC n Udnes, and Amund Fo ss in Udnes.) VIe. Sjonne?, who was manager of Slåstad in South Odal and whoowned 10 lispund in Middle Vågstad in Nes. VIf. Torris?, who was manager of Nes in Grue and who owned 1skin in Nes, 1 skin in Picksrud in Grue an
1 CONC d 8 skins (=10lispund) in Middle Vågstad. On the other hand, Søren of Vågstad was not a son of GisleSemmingsen. There were 10 lispund of South Vågstad that Sørenowned in 1615. In a sealed document he stated that S.A. EmbretTostensen Valstad wa
1 CONC s a part owner of all farm goods (23 lispundin 1647) in South Vågstad and that there was a lien in a 1663-64lawsuit with Thomas Thomesen Holt in Ullensaker. Semming, Nels, Otter and Marie were provable children of GisleSemmingsen. Sjonne and Torri
1 CONC s were probably either sons orsons-in-law.
